    <task id="LOCAL-00143" summary="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.5.17b Feb 14th 23:49&#10;&#10;Ray Tracing now actually renders to the MSAA HDR texture!&#10;That means you can see its shadows!&#10;&#10;I upsample the raw raytraced half-resolution texture and smooth the edges, then apply it to the MSAA HDR texture.&#10;&#10;The smoothing part needs some good work, but I am getting there.&#10;Tomorrow I will sort this out using TAA (NOT SHITTY Unreal Engine TAA, but my awesome TAA!)&#10;&#10;&#10;Changed an option in settings.toml to ShadowType, with OFF, CSM and RT options!&#10;&#10;I will also improve the CSM shadows with PCF, because CSM seems dirt cheap at 2048 and doesn't look half bad.&#10;If I strip out the old PCF and put in proper PCF, it will actually look good and fellow city builders on low-end hardware will still enjoy some sort of nice shadows!&#10;&#10;Made every shader use #include &quot;includes/uniforms.wgsl&quot; to avoid desynchronizing the Uniforms when I update them, and basically remove duplicates!&#10;&#10;I forgot to tell you some commits ago in .15 that I fixed water not rendering. Or did I forget? idk.&#10;&#10;***&#10;Cars 19  Carlos. Was machst du? Wo bist du? Wo ist Linus? Moroc??">
      <option name="closed" value="true" />
