      <updated>1771191344039</updated>
    </task>
    <task id="LOCAL-00145" summary="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.5.19a Feb 16th 23:13&#10;&#10;[Major]&#10;Fixed Intersections nearly COMPLETELY, they are the best they have ever been, clipper and earcutr do a very good job.&#10;Fixed a bug in the road editing where building a road at a shallow angle can cause the editor to think that it hits a road, when really, it is just the road that I am building away from! But actually, that should be possible, with curved roads for example... &#10;I will need to check it out again and find a better fix. &#10;&#10;Fixed huge bug in my WorldPos delta_to() helper, where the subject and object was flipped!&#10;So I had to fix some other areas that used this.&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;[Minor]&#10;Made RT shadows brighter.&#10;&#10;Node actually update their ARMS now, when added and when involved in MakeIntersection!&#10;&#10;***&#10;I am now prouder of my intersections than Donald Trump is of America, so not proud at all (HAHA MAGA, sorry, just a joke, really)&#10;&#10;Intersection issues where a total clusterfuck coming from a cataclysm of bugs in my game lol.&#10;&#10;It is SO refreshing seeing nearly PERFECT intersections, when before I had complete GARBAGE with a weird method I thought of in my sleep... &#10;This method I am using now, with clipper2 and earcutr (shoutout to all the devs there, heroes maintaining a dying codebase (C++ side is hanging in there by a thread for ClipperSys)) is WAY better and consistent.">
