    <task id="LOCAL-00156" summary="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.6.8a March 5th 23:43&#10;&#10;[Major]&#10;Rects have rotation and border color now.&#10;&#10;First instance of the checkbox working.&#10;The checkbox toggle when you click it! It syncs with its reference setting, so its state is always correctly representative of the setting!&#10;&#10;Override mode actually works now. (To edit uneditable elements, like the elements you might interact with from the editor menu to edit stuff)&#10;&#10;Merged all set actions into one and provided functionality for the other add, sub, mul etc. actions (unfinished, WIP)&#10;&#10;Added Hovering TouchEvent&#10;&#10;[Minor]&#10;Renamed all the wrong &quot;AV&quot; to &quot;AP&quot; because it is called Advanced Primitive, not V! CP2077 reference.&#10;&#10;Added editable option to the advanced primitive.&#10;&#10;Renamed action to actions, because I changed how actions are stored. Instead of just one String, it stores a Vec of Strings, you can type it way more explicitly now in YAML.&#10;&#10;You can write an action value explicitly using type:value (without spaces), like bool:false or set_setting_to(ap, string:hello how are you)!&#10;&#10;Refined some naming of actions and added Cycling of Enums Logic, including the new CyclePrev.&#10;&#10;***&#10;Solid shit.">
      <option name="closed" value="true" />
      <created>1772751413916</created>
      <option name="number" value="00156" />
      <option name="presentableId" value="LOCAL-00156" />
      <option name="project" value="LOCAL" />
      <updated>1772751413916</updated>
    </task>
    <task id="LOCAL-00157" summary="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.6.9a March 8th 23:29&#10;&#10;[Major]&#10;Removed the wrappers like &quot;on_release() in favor of &quot;on:&lt;condition&gt;&quot;, docs will follow later, no one uses my game anyway but me for now. &#10;2 Stars and I will write docs lol!&#10;&#10;Ok so&#10;Added &quot;on:TouchEventKind&quot;&#10;Added &quot;in:GameMode&quot; (or other environments)&#10;Added &quot;button:MouseButton&quot;&#10;&#10;Added a global actions file to have actions globally for all elements, like right-clicking on an element opening te color picker.&#10;&#10;Changed the Input system to track every mouse button, not just left.&#10;As you can see, actions can now be run on any mouse button and any TouchEventKind and environment.&#10;&#10;Copy, Paste and Cut now actually give and take the clipboard to and from the OS!&#10;&#10;&#10;[Minor]&#10;Fixed Rect hitbox and rendering half size bs (Was actually confusing it with clearance slack, which was the actual issue, it was adding 10.0 so that small elements could be clicked, but that led to an inaccurate hitbox confusing me!)&#10;Fixed Rect roundness&#10;&#10;Hovering over a UI element makes it impossible to click in the 3D environment.&#10;&#10;A text can display the name of the Setting an AP is referencing using the &quot;{ap}&quot; &quot;variable&quot;&#10;&#10;AP elements now properly offset from the AP coords, instead of defining it themselves (was overwritten by the AP coords anyway, so all elements where in the same spot until I fixed this.)&#10;&#10;***&#10;I FEEL ALIVE!!! -Heisenberg (the scientist(they are both scientists?) button:middle)&#10;&#10;NOTE TO MY FUTURE SELF: You edit an element in editor mode. Right click on it and the color picker pops up. &#10;Now, you can't edit the color picker because its elements are set to not be editable. &#10;But then you turn on override mode with F7 and you can now edit the color picker. &#10;Right-clicking an element of the Color picker with the override mode will open a color picker. But that is not the original color picker, but a cloned one with HARD uneditable flag turned on! This way you can edit the editing tool and use the editing tool while doing so, crazy, right?&#10;&#10;We got 500, 10, 25, 30, 40, 50 cool song on AFNEagle Bavaria.&#10;I voted today. Voted for tons of IT fellas idk anything about, voted on HUGE voting papers with like 92 votes!">
      <option name="closed" value="true" />
      <created>1773010364239</created>
      <option name="number" value="00157" />
      <option name="presentableId" value="LOCAL-00157" />
      <option name="project" value="LOCAL" />
      <updated>1773010364239</updated>
    </task>
    <task id="LOCAL-00158" summary="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.6.10a March 11th 23:21&#10;&#10;[Major]&#10;Value Parsing parses very properly now, resolving to settings values and Variable values now, updated all to 64bit values, including the entire Variables (I renamed it from UiVariableRegistry, wasn't so catchy was it?).&#10;&#10;If and IfVarEq seem to actually work now, I hope they do!&#10;&#10;You can toggle the Debug Menu with F3 now! &#10;&#10;Fixed Rect Border and made it use the Border Color.&#10;&#10;[Minor]&#10;Added little shit MainMenu with just a Play button that opens up to the game!&#10;&#10;Added back to the main menu keybind, game only exits at &quot;Leave Game&quot; keybind press once you are in the main menu. Both are ESC right now and forever.&#10;&#10;Removed some debug GUI elements.&#10;Replaced CommandArg with UiValue in the backend, just behind the scenes, really.&#10;Removed the useless variables system in favor of the single Variables system I already have, so now the variables are accessible everywhere.&#10;Completely removed wrappers in favor of filters (in:, on:, button:, etc...)&#10;&#10;Added on:desel and on:sel for selection based actions.&#10;Letting an action run while in editor_mode must be explicitly stated using in:editor_mode now.&#10;&#10;Moved Pick Position update from simulation to render, now roads and anything else doesn't lag and jump around while moving.&#10;&#10;Dragging text no longer selects text while doing so (I mean it only happened when you were wildly swinging the text around!)&#10;&#10;Replaced JetBrainsMono-Regular.ttf with Inter-Regular.ttf, complete text rendering overhaul coming up.&#10;&#10;***&#10;Just like in Minecraft!! &#10;Investigated water not reflecting, what an asshole, why doesn't it reflect?&#10;I think it should reflect on its life choices and film a former apology.&#10;Not with a ukulele though!&#10;DanTDM is good why did I just think of him, huh?? Baseball huh.">
      <option name="closed" value="true" />
      <created>1773269293570</created>
      <option name="number" value="00158" />
      <option name="presentableId" value="LOCAL-00158" />
      <option name="project" value="LOCAL" />
      <updated>1773269293571</updated>
    </task>
    <task id="LOCAL-00159" summary="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.6.11a March 12th 23:31&#10;&#10;[Major]&#10;Fixed water not reflecting the sun and the moon.&#10;&#10;[Minor]&#10;Added tiny settings menu&#10;Added exit button and exit command&#10;&#10;***&#10;it was a banal error: I added a mat4x4 for the stars to the sky uniforms, but forgot to change the struct in the water shader! So garbage info did its job.">
