    <task id="LOCAL-00160" summary="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.6.12a March 14th 20:07 PI DAY!!&#10;&#10;[Major]&#10;Changed the entire Text Rendering Backend from my own to wgpu-text, more reliable and robust.&#10;&#10;Text Anchors work properly again, Center is the default and the best imo&#10;&#10;Text can now be line-broken! You can press enter to make a line break! Or even write '\n'!&#10;&#10;Major for Wayland users (like me): Now supporting the 'wayland-data-control' feature on arboard, so Copying and pasting and cutting is actually reliable now on Wayland! All other OS's shouldn't have had the issue in the first place.&#10;&#10;[Minor]&#10;I changed 'px' to 'pt' in the YAML for the texts, because pt is more standard and more correct to work with.&#10;&#10;Fixed the UI Snap Modifier key not working&#10;&#10;You can maneuver inside the text with up and down arrows now, jumping between lines just like in any other program. &#10;Pasting also carries over the line breaks!&#10;You can press TAB to add 4 spaces, just like in programming IDEs.&#10;&#10;Now, selecting another text causes the other text that was just selected to EXIT editing mode instead of lingering weirdly!&#10;Also, now text can't be edited while editing (while writing text kind of editing).&#10;&#10;&#10;***&#10;Basically redid all the Text rendering stuff, so reliable now!!&#10;WARIO: EXCELLENTE!! Where is smigifour? Spongiform?? Weird-ass JetBrains autocorrect  &#10;Oh btw, it is PI DAY!!! Let's go! &#10;Top 3.14 uses of PI in my game:&#10;1. Circle shader&#10;2. Road node circle mesh&#10;3. Polygon Shader for rounding&#10;4. In the-">
