    <task id="LOCAL-00161" summary="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.6.13a March 15th 23:09 NOT PI DAY!!&#10;&#10;[Major]&#10;Made entire prop rendering system and already render trees. (Not spawned yet)&#10;It is instanced, of course and procedural, of course!&#10;You can place trees using the new 'Props' cursor mode.&#10;&#10;[Minor]&#10;Changed how the Cursor mode stores data, like prop name or road specs.&#10;&#10;Renamed more structs to simpler names. Like 'CarSubsystem' to 'Cars' and 'RoadSubsystem' to 'Roads' and 'AstronomyState' to just 'Astronomy'.&#10;Uselessly long names are horrible to code and look at.&#10;&#10;You can fetch the state of a setting using a variable in text like normal. &#10;If the variable name you typed matches the setting name, you get the value! No underscores exist in the settings btw&#10;&#10;Upgraded the CarChunkDistance and WorldPos::dist2() to 64 bit values.&#10;&#10;***&#10;Not pi day, but 15 day. half month day i guess? &#10;random-ass day but cool day, prop day i shall call it! where is my CAPS HUH HOW DO I TURN THIS OFF?? OK IF I CAN'T TURN IT OFF; &#10;THEN I WILL SCREAM OBSCENITIES: number 1: oh wait why did caps TURN OFF HOW IRONIC  THANKS FOR STICKING FOR MY PERFORMANCE; BYE!">
