    </task>
    <task id="LOCAL-00164" summary="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.6.16a March 28th 16:30&#10;&#10;wgpu updated to 29.0.1&#10;&#10;[Major]&#10;Added buildings struct and management which will render using the props' renderer.&#10;&#10;Fixed weirdness of polygon vertices management and storage and usage, now with a properly working scale value.&#10;&#10;Added action: set_expr(var, expr) which can do advanced arbitrary math using variables and constants and lots of functions, the same as the dynamic text uses. &#10;It sets to the variable after calculating.&#10;For this, I changed the whole backend to use just one Value enum, also supporting Arrays of Value!&#10;&#10;[Minor]&#10;Gave the trees a bark texture.&#10;&#10;Changed Syntax to not use the Pipe | symbol for function calls, but :   For example: fps|fix becomes fps:fix&#10;&#10;You can now index into an array variable by using .x, .y, .z, .r, .g, .b, .h, .s, .v, .0, .1, .2, .3, .4, .N...&#10;You can set a variable that contains dots now! like self.radius!&#10;&#10;Made the color picker picking color work, but only setting the variables for now, not the actual object color.&#10;The incredible thing about it is that I programmed that logic purely by using my actions system! &#10;Here are the actions I used:&#10;        actions:&#10;          - button:l, on:drag, in:editor_mode, set_expr(angle_shifted, atan2(mouse.y - self.center.y, mouse.x - self.center.x) + PI/2)&#10;          - button:l, on:drag, in:editor_mode, set_expr(color_picker_hsv.h, atan2(sin(angle_shifted), cos(angle_shifted)) / (2*PI) + 0.5)&#10;          - button:l, on:drag, in:editor_mode, set_expr(color_picker_hsv.s, sqrt((mouse.x - self.center.x)**2 + (mouse.y - self.center.y)**2) / self.radius)&#10;          - button:l, on:drag, in:editor_mode, set_expr(color_picker_color, hsv_to_rgb(color_picker_hsv.h, pow(color_picker_hsv.s, 0.47), 1.0))&#10;&#10;I am exposing info about the element calling the actions: self.radius, self.pt, self.center&#10;&#10;Renamed WorldCore to just World and the files too.&#10;&#10;Added new on: filter: 'on:drag' executed while dragging!&#10;&#10;***&#10;Cool worlds 2 And more cool space things. Bruh this game is crazy,">
      <option name="closed" value="true" />
      <created>1774714719604</created>
      <option name="number" value="00164" />
      <option name="presentableId" value="LOCAL-00164" />
      <option name="project" value="LOCAL" />
