    <task id="LOCAL-00165" summary="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.6.17a March 30th 22:28&#10;&#10;[Major]&#10;Overhauled selection system to consist of selected: Vec&lt;ElementRef&gt; and active_tool: Option&lt;ElementRef&gt; instead of primary and secondary crap.&#10;&#10;The color picker now actually colors elements!&#10;You can set colors using editing.color.*colorproperty*&#10;&#10;Made a new editability: HARDUNEDITABLE&#10;&#10;Very good side effect of overhauling selection: You can now PROPERLY select multiple elements and color ALL of them at once, or move all of them at once using wasd or even resize them!&#10;&#10;[Minor]&#10;Added Array parsing support so you can type in arrays in the YAML UI actions, and it parses correctly, like [1.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0]&#10;&#10;Advanced Primitive references are now persistent and are saved!&#10;&#10;IfVarEq now has an else branch and access to self and editing.&#10;&#10;Fixed all WRONG &quot;av&quot; instead of &quot;ap&quot;, replacing them with &quot;ap&quot;!! Annoying issue idk why I did that...&#10;&#10;Fixed some other things&#10;&#10;Layers now have editing_tool: bool to set if its elements can only be selected to the active_tool field.&#10;&#10;***&#10;GREAT WORLDS. Ostern, weird fucking name. Cool Worlds Alex Mc'Colgan is awesome! (sorry for butchering your name fr)">
