    <task id="LOCAL-00167" summary="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.6.19a April 6th 20:34&#10;&#10;[Major]&#10;PING PONG&#10;I finally made Ping pong solely in my UI System and no rust, just YAML! Try it!&#10;&#10;Fixed some major bug, 2 or so, which prevented me from making Ping pong!&#10;One was that I was parsing input Values when making the commands and then batched the commands, so setting a variable and then using it would yield an outdated value!&#10;Oh, and I just remembered the second bug:&#10;I used push_command() everywhere in the actions to do stuff on UI elements like setting self.center.x or other properties of an element, but that has the same issue as the first major bug, because the UI edit commands are run at the end of the frame, and sometimes you want to access the variable like self.center.x after you have updated it, but it hasn't updated yet!&#10;So I now use execute_command() instead, I have enough mutable access to do so, and it was an easy fix, fixing major headaches.&#10;&#10;&#10;[Minor]&#10;Expressions are now everywhere and predictable and less buggy!&#10;&#10;Added on:n which runs every frame.&#10;Added button:&quot;&quot; where you can type in a keybind or a key combo, and it will run while held! (Controllable using on:  ah wait actually no... Only holding is supported!)&#10;&#10;You can initialize variables if they don't exist now, using f64: before the variable for example, mostly in the set() command I think...&#10;&#10;on:down and on:d and on:hold now exist, they run while held!&#10;&#10;random() command added in expressions&#10;&#10;Way better error support here and there in actions and especially in the expression parser!&#10;&#10;Adding Integers and Floats now actually works!&#10;&#10;Mouse buttons can now be a modifier!&#10;&#10;self.size and self.color_components are now available.&#10;&#10;***&#10;POGGERS!! I dreamt of Dennis' house again today idk why, very random!&#10;Dennis is my dog&#10;Cat is my dog&#10;Dog is my cat and dennis is my cat&#10;and cat is dennis my&#10;and my banana is my dogs' dogs' banana cat in a sock!&#10;Did you understand?&#10;Understood?&#10;OVERstood?&#10;Alright you have overstood your welcome! (I didn't say welcome) I never said welcome. 20:57 already.">
