      <option name="presentableId" value="LOCAL-00170" />
      <option name="project" value="LOCAL" />
      <updated>1776109613479</updated>
    </task>
    <task id="LOCAL-00171" summary="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.7.2a April 20th 22:22&#10;&#10;[Major]&#10;Added Lots, which are the actual lots for houses.&#10;These lots have a width and length.&#10;You go into the zoning mode, then you will see lots of points on the sides of the roads.&#10;These points are where you can place the lot against.&#10;After you placed a lot, you can change its zone_type by simply clicking on the Lot with your desired ZoneType set on the cursor.&#10;It prevents you from placing if the lot collides with other lots or roads!&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;[Minor]&#10;Made astronomy more accurate, all use gmst now at 2026 01 01 00:00  Total game time is seconds since this date. Should match up with sun and moon irl and phases too.&#10;&#10;Zooming is now resistant to spam clicking and is always smooth because of it! L2 C2 Continuity?&#10;&#10;All meshed roads now give me RoadEdges so I can snap to them and test against them like in Lots!&#10;&#10;Made RoadType be stored in a RoadTypes storage and be accessed by an ID hash, so that the whole RoadType of 30 Bytes won't have to be cloned and stored in every single road element!&#10;I know, 30 bytes is tiny, but it's for the future and cleaner in code!&#10;&#10;The moon direction is now also shown on the gizmo.&#10;&#10;The gizmo now only shows when the debug menu is open. Like in MINECRAFT!!&#10;&#10;***&#10;I neglected the Area Zoning too from last update!&#10;&#10;Important: I gave up on Saving! Saving will only work for as many versions as it can, but it will break and I will care, but it's just way too hard to implement and not worth it!&#10;I will make saving better once Everything in the game is way more stable, like in Beta or even Pre release, it depends and we'll see!&#10;&#10;Not too much coding, lots of procrastination, at least I got something!">
      <option name="closed" value="true" />
      <created>1776719226370</created>
      <option name="number" value="00171" />
      <option name="presentableId" value="LOCAL-00171" />
      <option name="project" value="LOCAL" />
      <updated>1776719226370</updated>
    </task>
    <task id="LOCAL-00172" summary="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.7.3a April 29th 16:45&#10;&#10;Updated my rendering crate to 0.2.10&#10;Made first devlog: https://maxwag9.github.io/rusty_skylines_devlog/&#10;&#10;[Major]&#10;Area is now District.&#10;Districts spawn automatically when you zone a lot, but don't expand yet so all lots have their own district... &#10;&#10;Gizmo now has 3D TEXT rendering support!&#10;It looks really good, I made it have dynamic px scaling, and I am centering it and billboarding it so it always faces the camera!&#10;&#10;Added BLUR support to rect elements in UI! Looks awesome!&#10;&#10;&#10;[Minor]&#10;Made enums work in ui actions.&#10;Made tonemappingstate cyclable using a button in the settings menu.&#10;&#10;Updated Winit to the new beta version.&#10;&#10;***&#10;My Philosophy is that in an infinite World City builder like mine, zoning demand needs to be limited in the area it affects, or else the entire world will have one zoning demand and that would make no sense. &#10;For the players' convenience, I want districts to be automatically generated (or manually if you want, it's just the area tool).&#10;On every lot you zone, it checks if it is within or near a district and maybe gets itself included into its jurisdiction.&#10;When it doesn't find any, it will just make a new one with a default name (generated name, very simple).&#10;When a district gets too large or houses too many people or other reasons, it splits along roads, maybe.">
      <option name="closed" value="true" />
      <created>1777474727545</created>
      <option name="number" value="00172" />
      <option name="presentableId" value="LOCAL-00172" />
      <option name="project" value="LOCAL" />
      <updated>1777474727546</updated>
    </task>
    <task id="LOCAL-00173" summary="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.7.4a April 30th 16:56&#10;&#10;[Major]&#10;District splitting kinda works now. Buggy because it takes the road points directly though for now.&#10;&#10;Refactored half my game to use a global chunk size instead of passing it through every function!&#10;This is revolutionary for me, because this was such an insane nuisance!!&#10;&#10;Placing lots now spawns a new district at the lot if none is found in 100 meters from the lot, or, if found within 100m, it expands the closest district and adds itself to it!&#10;Like that, I ensure that the player doesn't need to worry about the districts while casually zoning.&#10;You can still manually make districts of course!&#10;&#10;[Minor]&#10;The gizmo text function has a new option to make the text be resized by the camera distance and fov.&#10;This happens to the district names, allowing you to see the names from far away.&#10;&#10;***&#10;Castor oil?? You want to burn me or what? Castjor means campfire in Russian, and then oil and then on my hairs, do you hear yourself? What if someone ignites me, huh? &#10;Then I will explode in flames because of the campfire oil in my hair wtf!!&#10;Get away from me, I'm calling Pest control!&#10;BTW I currently hold a fly captive in my jar.&#10;My cat is very interested in the jar all of a sudden, idk why!">
