    </task>
    <task id="LOCAL-00174" summary="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.7.5a May 1st 22:39&#10;&#10;Updated my wgpu_render_manager to 0.2.12.&#10;This update adds support for texture arrays, which I now use for the buildings.&#10;&#10;[Major]&#10;Added &quot;Buildings&quot; 👹🤮🤮.&#10;Ok ok chill, I just mean they are ugly right now, because I just made all buildings be an ugly purple cube with the &quot;goo&quot; texture so no wonder it looks horrendous!&#10;As I said, just for testing!&#10;It is an immense technical achievement though!&#10;I added the whole rendering for buildings aswell as shadows and a single place to make the chunk meshes!&#10;The buildings spawn on any lot that exists and that's about it.&#10;&#10;[Minor]&#10;Added GUI elements to add or decrease lanes that the cursor will build for the roads.&#10;&#10;***&#10;GUI looks garbage, procedural UI is hard. But tbh, I just haven't taken the time to make a proper GUI, even though that might be a good idea!! &#10;earcutr = &quot;0.5.0&quot; Bruh 30 DEPENDENCIES in my game this is insanity!">
