    <MESSAGE value="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.7.6a May 4th 22:22&#10;&#10;wgpu upgraded to 29.0.3&#10;&#10;[Major]&#10;Worked a bit further on the meshing of the buildings, separate for each zoning type.&#10;&#10;Added Tiles, which I want to be like the tiled procedural building system that Citystate: Metropolis showed off!&#10;Tiles are just either perfect squares that fit inside the lot, or polygons inside the lot.&#10;Each tile will have some kind of function in the building.&#10;One might just be a house, others make a garage and others are for the garden.&#10;They just outline how the building looks like!&#10;&#10;[Minor]&#10;Added 3 new textures: shingles.wgsl, metal_roof.wgsl and paint.wgsl.&#10;&#10;THINGS I FORGOT TO MENTION THAT I FIXED IN THE UPDATE BEFORE THE LAST ONE (1.7.4 maybe, maybe 1.7.3):&#10;1. The first road finally reliably gets its road edges, which enables it to be zoned and interacted with.&#10;Issue was that the preview roads pushed to the same road edge storage.&#10;That meant that the preview road you see when you drag to build a road had its segment ID 0 and was pushing it to the storage, so the real road couldn't push it.&#10;&#10;2. The Road mesh partly disappearing.&#10;My roads are meshed based on a chunk ID passed into the mesher.&#10;The issue was that the mesher would only include a vertex when it was actually in the chunk that the chunk ID refers to.&#10;And the Road Segment that is being chunked has only one chunk ID and spans multiple chunks, so some parts that were in chunks other than its own were left out.&#10;I just removed the chunk ID thing there, so the whole mesh spanning multiple chunks now includes only one chunk.&#10;Ok now I see that sounds kinda bad, so I might add it back and make a loop of chunks or something, nah a bit different, let's see!&#10;&#10;3. Fixed Node Meshing&#10;The nodes themselves are meshed using a triangle fan, which had a weird check in place for CCW or CW, and then it would flip the triangle.&#10;That caused the Back-face culling to cull some triangles sometimes, which means that holes would pop in and out of view.&#10;(I do understand that my explanation is wrong, cuz it is not the culling that is popping it in and out, cuz already built nodes didn't pop, but preview nodes which mesh every frame did!)&#10;&#10;Gizmo buffer overflow now just stops gizmo rendering instead of crashing. Not too much better but better nonetheless.&#10;&#10;Buildings render after Gizmo now to stop the trippy.&#10;&#10;Made lot and district area gizmo more transparent, less opaque yk.&#10;&#10;***&#10;Right now it looks like hot stinking garbage. Ah, no I actually deleted the hot stinking garbage, no building for you now!&#10;&#10;Mostly because I just wanted to test some more about variation and wanted to test the new textures, but AI can't deal with my WorldPos so it always codes in Vec3 like a maniac, but whatever.&#10;&#10;&#10;Crazy long explanation, but I witnessed amogus today. Which just means I said amogus in my head and with my mouth.&#10;&#10;Thanks for reading my essay on the elevation discrepancy between Alpha v1.7.5a and Alpha v1.7.6a! (Watch the Backrooms movie in theaters on 29th May 2026, it will be crazy, I hope Clark survives)" />
    <MESSAGE value="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.7.7a May 7th 22:53&#10;&#10;[Major]&#10;Lot tiles are now assigned TileTypes!&#10;TileType is something like 'House' or 'Driveway'&#10;&#10;The only ones that are meshed right now are 'House' and 'Driveway'! Coincidence?&#10;&#10;The building now is the same every time because I don't seed yet.&#10;the building has a driveway and the house Walls and a &quot;Roof&quot; on top of those walls, super simple just for testing.&#10;&#10;Fixed Issue: https://github.com/maxwag9/rusty_skylines/issues/10&#10;That issue affected mostly Mac users running Apple Silicon.&#10;The issue was that the WGPU feature 'TIMESTAMP_QUERY_INSIDE_PASSES' was not available on some GPUs like in Apple Silicon, so my game crashed.&#10;I put all the profiling at encoder level instead, so now I removed the feature and fixed the first ever issue!&#10;&#10;[Minor]&#10;New texture: driveway_bricks.wgsl&#10;&#10;UI hiding now actually works again, problem was that the UI frame texture was not cleared when hiding, which left the last image of UI on screen.&#10;&#10;Restructured some structs like Simulation and GameState to be owned by Resources instead of World, which allows me to pass the whole World to functions that need it while borrowing GameState like for example for saving and loading.&#10;&#10;Spawning buildings now update the residential zoning demand of the district. Invisible for now and doesn't affect a thing.&#10;&#10;Gizmo now renders LAST to stop the trippier trippy!&#10;&#10;Zoning is now not owned by Buildings, this will make borrowing easier.&#10;&#10;***&#10;Looks better than the Hot stinking Garbage houses&#10;Literally PC wasting time and electricity (and therefore my money) updating the zoning demand... Poor guy!&#10;In the last commit, instead of 'stop the trippy' I actually wanted to say 'stop the trippy feeling' or smth, but I forgot, but it's funny! Who cares" />
    <MESSAGE value="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.7.8a May 11th 23:19&#10;&#10;Updated my rendering crate to 0.2.14&#10;&#10;Huge terrain update&#10;&#10;[Major]&#10;Terrain is way more performant now, but still slow.&#10;Terrain is nearly fully async now, so no stutters at all! (Only when editing a new chunk though, but that's tiny)&#10;Moved meshing of terrain and edit application and stitching to the async workers!&#10;&#10;The terrain under houses now flattens and tapers off smoothly!! (Insane big refactor of the whole terrain system for this)&#10;&#10;The terrain edits are stored as TerrainEdit now, which is just an operation like Raise(amount) and similar! This will make save files way smaller and future-proof!&#10;Before this, edits were stored as all edited points, which is so wasteful and actually maybe slower than this method, in runtime?&#10;&#10;Oh right, The terrain refactor overshadowed it, but I also did:&#10;Roofs are now way more realistic, they actually look like roof, for example triangle roofs!&#10;&#10;&#10;[Minor]&#10;Fixed the annoying overlap of orbit control with arrow keys and the fast-forward/reverse of the simulation.&#10;FW/RV is now controlled with ',' and '.' because I ot no clue what else, and actually VLC Media Player uses them to skip single frames, I think.&#10;&#10;Also deactivated the car chunk update gizmo debug draw.&#10;That was there for maybe over 40 versions and idk, I have no use for it, and it pollutes the scene!&#10;&#10;New texture: wood_slab.wgsl&#10;Changed the grass.wgsl texture a bit and the texture keys for the terrain using grass.&#10;&#10;Added controller 'support'!&#10;That means that you can make keybinds for controllers, and it won't work!&#10;Idk why it won't, but I don't care right now. I mean, making the game actually have a game loop is way more important right now.&#10;The controller buttons do seem to register perfectly fine, it is just my conversion that is weird... low priority, just added out of curiosity, was super easy, thanks to gilrs!&#10;&#10;Flipped both axes of control of the Orbit with arrow keys.&#10;&#10;Each house is now actually randomized, seeded!&#10;Houses now have grass for the garden, and also TREES!&#10;Optimized house meshing severely. But not enough AT ALL!&#10;&#10;***&#10;Well? Found a motivated day today, haven't I! Spent the whole day on the goddamn terrain system, but also goddamn proud of myself for pulling through some of the BS!&#10;BS means BeatleS or BtS. NO, it means BULLSHIT.&#10;&#10;I palyed more CP2077, which means less content for you and less progress and yeah... that's not cool!!&#10;(Intentional misspelling as always-)&#10;Oh, by the way, my phone fell a second time this week and this time the panel actually got a lobotomy and started showing vertical lines, like on my old phone that broke! &#10;That wouldn't be such a big deal to me, if only it DIDN'T GENTLY FUCK UP THE TOUCHSCREEN on the left hand side, often letting me not click! &#10;But I can actually kind of use it, and scrcpy will be good for later!" />
    <MESSAGE value="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.7.9a May 13th 23:41&#10;&#10;[Major]&#10;Fixed 2 big UI bugs!&#10;1. Each AP template was added to the layers by every single AP reference, even if they didn't reference it!&#10;Such a strange and pretty STUPID error I did 2 months ago, but wtf for real??&#10;&#10;2. The AP reference is stored as an element in the elements list of each layer.&#10;During Cache initialization, I check if the length of this list in a layer has changed compared to its cache counterpart.&#10;I did not include the APs into this cache list, so the lengths were NEVER the same and the cache was reinitialized every frame, leading to that disgusting flickering I saw in the Settings menu all the time!&#10;The flickering is gone now. I included the AP Reference in the cache list, but it serves no function there, it's just another enum field.&#10;&#10;I added a schedule.rs file and hooked the economy and schedule structs up to the new CityState struct, which will hold per world stuff, like money and schedule and statistics and probably more!&#10;&#10;&#10;[Minor]&#10;Added a Residential Zoning Indicator, WIP as hell, and also it indicates the bugginess of my WIP residential zoning demand calculations!&#10;&#10;All zoning demand values for the closest district are now being set as variables, and are accessible to the UI as that! &#10;&#10;Fixed the on:always and on:a flags on UI actions!&#10;&#10;OH! I added a money indicator and in-game Time indicator!&#10;&#10;Made it clearer in the Terrain Edits who requested an edit. Like for example a building requested that the terrain underneath be flattened.&#10;&#10;The AP variable is now ap_var instead of setting, because now you can reference a variable instead of only settings, which expands capability DRAMATICALLY sometimes and actually yes, and also I dramatize!&#10;&#10;I quartered the individual page size for terrain from for example 256MB for just vertices per page, to 64MB per page. Still a lot, but less risk of fragmentation ruining dozens of millions of vertices. (Also quartered indices!)&#10;&#10;Refactored some Terrain Edit Types to use the height from WorldPos points that literally already exist instead of some weird heights.&#10;God, I hate AI for stuff like this... Fast as hell but has such oversights.&#10;&#10;&#10;***&#10;Anders Hellmann with one N?&#10;Btw I printed AMOGUS  I am going crazy I belong in a mental asy- no..." />
    <MESSAGE value="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.7.10a May 16th 23:46&#10;&#10;[Major]&#10;Added population!&#10;Added Demography and Education and LifeStages.&#10;&#10;Changed the meaning of time itself in the game.&#10;Now each day is 30 real life minutes long, 24 in game hours.&#10;20 Days per year and the average human lifespan is 23 years.&#10;This is major, because this is literally TIME! Don't you understand?&#10;This makes one year at single speed equal 10 real life hours. A decade is 100 hours.&#10;&#10;People now spawn into the city as you build more housing.&#10;Though, all the insight you get is only the new World Population counter in the bottom left!&#10;&#10;Demographics are saved in history so you can look back in the future when I implement it, how your population has changed. (Your actions matter &gt;:( )&#10;&#10;&#10;[Minor]&#10;World Population is shown on the GUI!&#10;Fixed AP text not being able to parse a {{ap}} to get the value behind the variable.&#10;&#10;Fixed astronomy, but also changed the year length so now it isn't like irl anymore....... :(&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;***&#10;println!(&quot;ADDED GUY!!&quot;); (real line)&#10;I had to compromise heavily on the year length in order to get the game somewhat playable!&#10;Because at real life snail speeds of time, the game would run as fast as real life, which would be insane.&#10;&#10;YES Finally we got people in the city! &quot;People&quot;! It's just numbers and chances!&#10;Literally just statistics.&#10;&#10;Anyways, this is awesome." />
    <MESSAGE value="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.7.11a May 18th 23:47&#10;&#10;[Major]&#10;You can now DESTROY houses and Roads!!&#10;Took me long enough...&#10;&#10;Destroying Roads shows a destruction preview!&#10;&#10;Made simulation better in some ways, mainly demand, but still not optimal. (Switched to deficit demand)&#10;&#10;Education stuff now actually updates (just add_person(), that's it!)&#10;&#10;[Minor]&#10;Added 13 more debug simulation values to the UI about the closest district.&#10;&#10;Added EducationLevel::None.&#10;&#10;Saving a world with an empty name now actually saves it as New World x&#10;&#10;Now I save the chunk positions of Lots for a fast query.&#10;&#10;***&#10;Mainly, the Destruction stuff took the longest! Way more complicated than imagined!&#10;Had to recursively disable nodes and segments and lanes until the deletion makes sense.&#10;&#10; Playstation 3 Ambient Jungle Mix&#10;Dopo Goto&#10;20.100 Abonnenten&#10;What more can I say. Feels empty. My mouth also feels empty." />
    <MESSAGE value="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.7.12a May 20th 23:33&#10;&#10;[Major]&#10;Fixed Road issues:&#10;1. Segment start and end nodes, where the segment gets split, were disabled, leading to them not being meshed and vanishing.&#10;2. Destruction preview doesn't include some nodes, so some segments that will be destroyed just don't show up on the preview.&#10;3. TRIED to fix the intersection flattening, I need just 10 minutes of time but don't have it!&#10;4. Kinda fixed corridor length calculation mismatch between the intersection geometry call site and the meshing call site. &#10;I unified them, which means I calculate the corridor lengths ONCE when gathering the intersection arms, then store them in their respective arms.&#10;I still saw some issues, so might have to tinker a bit more, but mostly kinda fixed.&#10;&#10;&#10;Made intersections use the road_type data of each segment instead of their own, which makes the intersections look more correct because it actually meshes from each different arm of the intersection.&#10;&#10;Made terrain better.&#10;The terrain is now like before, but better. So continents exist again, mountains exist again, some new beach stuff exists, but it's all still shit. XD :(&#10;&#10;[Minor]&#10;Experimented making a terrain &quot;Map&quot; (Literally nothing changed in-game)&#10;EXTREMELY early stage, don't get hyped.&#10;&#10;Preview Roads now DON'T rebuild every frame.&#10;&#10;***&#10;Smaller update.&#10;I DON'T HAVE TIME FOR FOOTNOTES SHIT 23:59" />
    <MESSAGE value="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.7.13a May 23rd 17:18&#10;&#10;[Major]&#10;The terrain now mixes in a rock texture smoothly when the terrain is steeper. &#10;&#10;The intersection flattening is now sloped, so it becomes less of a sharp transition.&#10;ALSO, I am now flushing dirty chunks immediately after flattening, so the segments which are created after the flattening actually use the flattened terrain heights immediately.&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;[Minor]&#10;Added render_node_ids_gizmo.&#10;Added a stub signfinding.rs file.&#10;A garage now only spawns in residential lots.&#10;&#10;Interesting update: changed the ChunkId from zigzag calculations to simple packing of chunk coords (i32, i32) into u64.&#10;Should improve performance slightly here and there, but probably immeasurable. BUT it costs like 10x less to create the ChunkId from ChunkCoords now!&#10;The locality of the ID isn't important to me anymore.&#10;&#10;Removing a lot or building now also removes the flattening of the terrain under it (literally did this just now)&#10;&#10;***&#10;This is a transfer commit to my laptop cuz I am going to Turkey.&#10;&#10;The rock texture on the terrain looks awesome, it gives the Cities Skylines feel tbh." />
    <MESSAGE value="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.7.14a May 31st 22:43&#10;&#10;[Major]&#10;*Signfinding Section Start*&#10;Changed the Partition System COMPLETELY from hierarchical partitions referencing Nodes.&#10;Instead, each partition now stores up to 20 BuildingIds so they are bundled together for a WAY easier signfinding implementation.&#10;&#10;Added functions to the Arm of a Node that extract the travel time (EMA ExponentialMovingAverage) properly, with BuildingId first, PartitionId second and DistrictId last.&#10;&#10;Added a function that ranks the best arms for an intersection (node ofc).&#10;*Signfinding Section End*&#10;&#10;&#10;[Minor]&#10;Placing lots now searches for roads in a 3x3 chunk radius instead of only the mouse chunk.&#10;&#10;Placing lots also now shows only road points in a radius instead of all road points of a road. Performance is heavily improved by doing so!&#10;&#10;Now adding and removing car spawning road nodes when nodes get enabled or disabled.&#10;&#10;Settings menu UI now has all gizmo options available.&#10;&#10;Partition Gizmo is now completely different, adapted to the new Partitions system.&#10;&#10;Drag-Removing Buildings and Lots is now possible (buggy, buildings or lots reappear for some reason?!)&#10;&#10;***&#10;Gib mir doggy gib mir doggy gib mir doggy... SPAẞ ich bin ein Mann und ich bin nicht schwul!!&#10;Sorry for this German throw-up.&#10;&#10;The Signfinding is progressing!&#10;I came from my vacation in Turkey, best vacation yet imo.&#10;At 19 yrs old, it feels different!&#10;Constantly went to the Sauna and Beach (Antalya)&#10;The hotel was the Kremlin Palast Hotel near Lara.&#10;&#10;Ok cool. I will go to sleep soon!&#10;So, May basically? May is over and my game has grown.&#10;Each month, my game becomes better!&#10;I looked at the releases on GitHub I've built (the executables) and my game really has improved dramatically!&#10;So much so that I get a feeling of dread when I look at my old releases, because I am just imagining myself back then not knowing wtf happens months later and just working through the problems I have worked through before!&#10;And I AM the before right now! Always am..." />
    <MESSAGE value="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.7.15a June 3rd 23:04&#10;&#10;[Major]&#10;*Signfinding Section Start*&#10;Implemented Signfinding roughly, no breadcrumbs are spread yet (I literally forgot to do that)&#10;*Signfinding Section End*&#10;&#10;Completely refactored the Car physics trajectory calculation and sf trajectory is calculated now to. (sf is signfinding)&#10;&#10;&#10;[Minor]&#10;Added gizmo rendering for signfinding, showing you the current extent of the physical trajectory and the path of the sf trajectory.&#10;&#10;Finally fixed UI state synchronization.&#10;To fix it, I added a new on:activated and on:deactivated filters on actions.&#10;Using those filters, you can set for example a checkbox to update its visual state at the exact moment it appears on screen when it activates. (I did that with my checkbox)&#10;So now all checkboxes show the real current state.&#10;&#10;Removed the index 0 restriction from all storages in my game, so now index 0 is usable again (it was literally always usable, because the placeholder was overwritten )&#10;&#10;Removed useless pathfinding fields in lanes and nodelanes.&#10;&#10;Lanes are wider now. from 3.1m to 3.6m now.&#10;&#10;I am now keeping track of where the cars are on the road, so I can know O(1).&#10;&#10;***&#10;Commit situation is insane&#10;Signfinding situation is insane&#10;(btw if you are uncultured and don't get it, moistcritikal/penguinz0 titles all his videos &quot;xyz situation is insane&quot;)&#10;Gigantic commit. Lots of work and BRAINZ (The Z is important, because this work zombifies my brain)&#10;&#10;The most major things get the least words... Why is that?&#10;&#10;Most of my time was spent on figuring out how to implement signfinding...&#10;And then the even harder physics trajectory calculation!&#10;Signfinding is just giving turns and the physics is actually converting them to holding distance to cars in front, accelerating, steering, following the lane, in the future: &#10;Parking, following the NodeLane at an intersection, stopping and going at traffic lights, changing lanes, yielding, turn signals my god so much to do and that's good, cuz that means POTENTIAL!!&#10;&#10;Feels like there should be more in this commit, but there isn't! All my effort went into the signfinding on the 2nd of June and physics on the 3rd of June!&#10;now 23:28, it took me 24 mins to write this commit..." />
    <MESSAGE value="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.7.16a June 10th 22:31&#10;&#10;[Major]&#10;*Signfinding Section Start*&#10;No breadcrumbs yet.&#10;Refactored every tiny part of the sf_traj and phys_traj functions.&#10;Found many issues and shifted philosophy.&#10;Shifted from sf_traj providing next arm of intersection as the turn, to sf_traj providing every possible lane of the Segment or every possible path through the intersection.&#10;So now a 'turn' is one of two things: A Segment or an Intersection.&#10;This way I shift more load to the sf_traj function in finding all possible paths, while also maintaining the power of the phys_traj to change lanes and paths.&#10;Phys_traj now uses at most one lane or nodelane as its path, and ends prematurely when reaching the last point of the laneref, causing the next turn and laneref to be pathed.&#10;*Signfinding Section End*&#10;&#10;Cars now spawn at buildings! Factors controlling spawning include: Time of day, Zone type of building, a random age based on demography, traffic multiplier, and number of tenants.&#10;(The age part is buggy right now, I need to fix it, just saw that it is buggy, shifted toward 3x the Max age.)&#10;It then spawns a car at a random address based on what the trip type is and preferring closer commutes.  (Only destinations supported are workplaces, which are Offices, commercial and industrial.)&#10;This is done per district tick (1.0s per tick for a district), which leads us cleanly to the next topic:&#10;Refactored district ticking completely.&#10;Districts are now ticked in a rayon parallel iterator.&#10;&#10;I now keep track of prop instances of a building, so they can get removed properly when rebuilding a BuildingChunk or removing a building.&#10;This fixes dozens of trees and other props spawning over time as the building chunk gets rebuilt multiple times.&#10;Completely reworked how props are stored, now functioning like any of my other storages, Vec with id == idx and O(1). Archetypes are also stored this way now.&#10;&#10;Improved trajectory error passthrough immensely.&#10;&#10;I am allowing U turns at dead ends now.&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;[Minor]&#10;Added setting and checkbox to toggle simple_car_following, which controls whether the cars use physics and IDM to follow the lanes or simple: just follow them by snapping to the points of the path!&#10;&#10;Heavily simplified the signature of building spawning and despawning functions and the props getter and placing functions.&#10;&#10;Lots of new Gizmo for information on signfinding and trajectory stuff:&#10;Seg_id shown above segments, Lane_id shown above lanes, Nodelane_id and node_id and merging/splitting lanes shown above nodelanes, phys_traj of car shown as arrows, sf_traj shown as arrows, car.last_turn and car.current_lane shown above car!&#10;&#10;Simplified the Address to just building_id. Now inferring partition and district from building.&#10;&#10;I am using 'tracing' now, but probably not often, I don't plan to log using it yet, I am a println!() kind of guy!&#10;I am now actually progressing the schedule based on time of day.&#10;&#10;Split districts now reference the correct lot ids.&#10;&#10;Added transports.rs file, which holds the TransportStats, unused for now, but will hold the stats for the traffic, like commute counts or shopping counts or transporting trucks count... Basically which trips have been randomly selected when we spawned a car.&#10;&#10;***&#10;Basically worked on the signfinding and physical trajectory creation this whole week.&#10;It was super hard, but finally got them driving kinda properly.&#10;&#10;Huh, interesting... So people with low IQ would prefer a medium IQ leader over a high IQ leader? Relatively speaking of course. Reminds me of Donald Trump&#10;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yk4XMhqwz6E" />
    <MESSAGE value="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.7.17a June 12th 22:55&#10;&#10;[Major]&#10;Taxes are now implemented! It is progressively taxing people.&#10;&#10;Building Roads costs MONEY!!&#10;When you build a road now, it will calculate the cost based on length, road type and width, and crossings! Intersections are of course an added cost, +20% per intersection! (I should change it to absolute instead of relative!)&#10;And then it will show you as a 3D text, how much money it costs and how long that road is.&#10;&#10;ALSO implemented REFUNDS!&#10;You can go into destruction mode and preview the destruction, showing you the Refund amount that you will get back, in 3D gizmo text!&#10;The refund is 15% of the building value of the roads, excluding crossings!&#10;&#10;Refactored the 3D text gizmo system quite a bit.&#10;In particular how it acquires glyphs and uses them.&#10;My problem was that some 3D text would flicker and disappear!&#10;The reason was because glyph_brush only computed the glyphs once and not again! &#10;Because it is so keen on caching, it hashes the text and its info and then gives new glyphs, or if already calculated, just tells you: &quot;Fuck you! You saved the glyphs for later, right? You are caching, right? Cuz I won't give you anything! HAHA!! Deal with it, moron!&quot; and just leaves me with an Ok(BrushAction::ReDraw).&#10;So I did what it asked me to do. And now with caching, 3d text performance should be like 3-5x better on the CPU. But I am not sure if it's really this much better.&#10;&#10;[Minor]&#10;Moved instance id texture creation to its own pass, but then decided to just comment it out cuz it's just too hard to do, but then RIGHT NOW as I am writing this, I thought about it and just reenabled it, changed some things, compiles, ok. &#10;But I bet it now doesn't work in some way, because I didn't put a depth attachment in place for now... Now the Issue by ProhorTaim should be fixed, maybe. &#10;Maybe the motion texture is also an issue? &#10;I mean it shouldn't, because msaa should be able to resolve Rg16Float, but it couldn't do u32 ofc, cuz, what's the average of 4 u32s? &#10;You might think &quot;easy&quot;, but the wgpu spec and especially the metal spec seem to think that you can't average them. We users have no control. You can't just tell him to &quot;Just take the first sample and that's your pixel!&quot;...…&#10;Because of this, I need to collect the props again, which doubles the props cpu time partially.&#10;&#10;Money is now i64 instead of f64, screw the cents.&#10;&#10;Tried to make the ends of thick gizmo lines be rounded instead of square, but something is wrong with the function making them, so they don't render, but just render super weirdly. &#10;&#10;Moved time and money texts apart in the GUI so that lots of money can be shown. (mrbeast)&#10;Every world starts with 2_000_000€ now.&#10;&#10;Removed the red filled area rendering where a road is going to be destroyed, because the road preview does it anyway.&#10;&#10;***&#10;Note to myself to un-hardcode the screen size value in the thick_lines.wgsl shader.&#10;This felt fast. Did the taxes and road buying yesterday, refunds and gizmo crap today. Good progress.&#10;Audi A6&#10;The whole tax system is vibe coded as fuck, but works for now. Saves me loads of time. Claude is good (free Claude)&#10;    /// It works, but I am still mad at glyph_brush. Nothing personal, just pain." />
    <MESSAGE value="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.7.18a June 19th 23:05&#10;&#10;[Major]&#10;Fixed issue #11, so Crash doesn't happen anymore.&#10;&#10;Made the DROP-DOWN!!&#10;The Dropdown is coded natively in YAML, which was the hardest thing to do yet, requiring lots of changes to APs, UI Commands and especially the parsing of values/names/arguments of the UI commands.&#10;Because of these changes, every single value-based UI element broke, not displaying the values properly anymore.&#10;That's because I changed the UI text element text field parsing from proprietary, to being the same parser that the rest of UI uses, so it doesn't have the modifiers it had before, so it fails to parse! Sorry!&#10;I am going to fix this in the next update, but for now it's broken like that. Hauptsache I made the Dropdown menu work!&#10;You can find it in the Settings menu, and it works flawlessly in my testing!&#10;&#10;[Minor]&#10;You can't move or change orbit zoom while your mouse is over a UI element anymore.&#10;Scroll Events now actually work outside of editor mode.&#10;Added and removed UI commands.&#10;Wrote much more documentation for my UI system, now out of date.&#10;Fixed UI events limit being just 64 events in queue&#10;&#10;***&#10;The Spooky Scary Dropdown Menu was always my final boss with my UI.&#10;And I finally made it work! With many casualties and 7 days on the way, just for a dropdown menu!&#10;In coding, the easiest things are the hardest. and the hardest thing are the hardest too. EVERYTHING IS HARD! Nah, not always...&#10;Let me tell you about the Dropdown menu, I should make it worthwhile:&#10;You go into the settings menu and see the gloryful dropdown.&#10;You see it says &quot;tonemapping_state: Night&quot;, you click on it, and it POPS UP into 6 options underneath!&#10;You tremble out of fear cuz you just got spooked, then you adjust your +13.5 glasses and look at the options: 'Cinematic', 'Golden hour' and more.&#10;&quot;Interesting!!&quot;, you exclaim while you tip your fedora (but u use arch, not fedora, what a liar).&#10;You click on the Option 'Cinematic' and cluckcluckcluckcluckcluck, the options disappear and now it says &quot;tonemapping_state: Cinematic&quot;!&#10;&#10;Commit long enough yet?&#10;Here's the technical detail of how it works:&#10;If you click on the dropdown AP, it toggles {ap}_open, then checks if it is true.&#10;If so, it will iterate the {ap}.options and add_ap() into its own menu, under distinct names like {ap}_Option_{idx}, just enough under it to get clearance, with the ap_var being {ap}.options.{idx} and the ap_name being &quot;dropdown_option&quot;.&#10;So then they spawn and then each option checks if you clicked on them and turns the {ap}_open to false and iterates and deletes the aps if false. And sets the setting to the value ofc.&#10;The big issue slowing this whole thing down was that I need to split the ap_var into parts by '.' to get access to the {ap}, so that I have the string &quot;tonemapping_state&quot; somehow.&#10;Here's how I get it: 'strexpr:{split(&quot;{ap}&quot;, &quot;.&quot;).0}_open' At least it works. There is much more detail, but hell nah.&#10;This week spent on UI better be worth it, and it is!&#10;BTW you can scroll on the dropdown to cycle the options! Most irl dropdowns don't even have that...&#10;OH and btw! ALL colors from the colors file are now broken cuz of the parsing! So zoning and more don't render at all! Brilliant!!" />
    <MESSAGE value="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.7.19a June 21st 23:16&#10;&#10;[Major]&#10;Tried to fix issue #11 Part 3, maybe fixed, probably not, cuz macOS is a strict mom, added loads of print!() to identify the exact issue&#10;&#10;Fixed all UI issues from last time.&#10;Fixed the broken colors, which weren't broken, so the lot system wasn't broken!&#10;It just appeared to not render to me, but the actual real problem was the thick gizmo lines rendering completely mangled and wrong, also with thickness in pixel space, while I am giving it in world space!&#10;So I fixed that, and now the BEAUTIFUL Thick lines render perfectly, with AA corners, no sharp crap like before!&#10;&#10;[Minor]&#10;Added :.n support to the expression parser.&#10;&#10;Zoning Demand Indicator now renders green bar filling from bottom to top, instead of from center up and down.&#10;I also put the zoning demand number into the green space and made it red.&#10;&#10;More helpful actions error messages when setting an element variable.&#10;&#10;***&#10;Basically, this release is courtesy of @ProhorTaim, whatever &quot;courtesy of&quot; even means...&#10;It's for him to test." />
    <MESSAGE value="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.8.0a June 29th 23:50&#10;&#10;[Major]&#10;Improved the simulation immensely.&#10;I track every citizen now, but not as actual persons, but as statistical people.&#10;So basically every building stores its own count of tenants and employment and demography and education counts, which are counted together to form the district-wide demography.&#10;This makes the location of buildings actually mean something (and land value means more ofc) and all future simulation relies on this locationality.&#10;Or else the whole district would be the same.&#10;&#10;Maybe fixed infinite remeshing of buildings bug.&#10;&#10;Maybe fixed Issue #11.&#10;Maybe, cuz I fixed it by drawing the tonemapped final image to the swapchain directly instead of copying it over.&#10;&#10;Corporations are taxed now too&#10;&#10;Just all around major changes to simulation I don't have time to write the commit sadly.&#10;&#10;[Minor]&#10;Fixed always_day&#10;&#10;Added Milestones screen for 300 population and more, softlocks you!!!&#10;&#10;Made UI Blur fancier&#10;&#10;Ficed initialization of variables in UI parser.&#10;&#10;***&#10;Lots of work this week with two parts of my family moving at the same time lol. Luckily to Ground floor, but from 3rd or 4th floor!" />
    <MESSAGE value="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.8.2a July 15th 22:31&#10;&#10;[Major]&#10;Fixed some of the legacy road crashes from before, a lot still remains.&#10;&#10;Fixed major UI parsing issue, now pingpong and zoning demand indicators work again!&#10;&#10;[Minor]&#10;Fixed some parking things, but the car freezes when in parking mode, so until later!&#10;&#10;Added knockback to the paddles in the Ping Pong menu.&#10;Added ball squish when it touches the paddles in the Ping Pong menu.&#10;&#10;The set zoning type buttons now switch the cursor mode to zoning.&#10;&#10;***&#10;That's kind of it? Bruh.&#10;&#10;Signed-off-by: maxwag9 &lt;maximwagner46@gmail.com&gt;" />
    <MESSAGE value="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.8.3a July 23rd 23:16&#10;&#10;Major boulderous UI update!&#10;&#10;[Major]&#10;&#10;&#10;[Minor]&#10;&#10;&#10;***" />
    <MESSAGE value="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.8.3a July 23rd 23:16&#10;&#10;Major boulderous UI update!&#10;&#10;[Major]&#10;HUGE update:&#10;Added SAVING, well, it was there before, but now it will NOT break saves every single version!&#10;That's because I have found the SAINT called &quot;revision&quot;, which is a Rust crate to do versioned saves so I can just set the revisions when I change something, so that saves don't break!&#10;&#10;Added UI action filter 'as:', use like:&#10;'- in:any button:any as:[&quot;overlay&quot;, &quot;add&quot;], set(str:self.center, {as.center}); set(str:self.color.fill, [1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0]);'&#10;The 'as:' filter does not run the command on the element, it only exposes the fields of the as element!&#10;The array can contain 1, 2 or 3 arguments.&#10;With 3 arguments, it is [menu_name, layer_name, element_id].&#10;With 2 arguments, it is [layer_name, element_id]. And here, the menu is substituted using 'self.menu'.&#10;With 1 argument, it is [element_id].              And here, menu is 'self.menu' and layer is 'self.layer'!&#10;&#10;Changed global actions to be split between:&#10;element_actions: being actions that are literally run by every element in the universe&#10;global_actions: being actions that are run without a self element context, as is supported though, but discouraged. Modders will use anyway.&#10;&#10;Layers can now have actions too! That includes advanced primitives, because they are just layers underneath anyway.&#10;&#10;Fixed some hugely annoying bugs.&#10;&#10;Added call() action! You can define a &quot;function&quot; by setting a variable as text like this:&#10;'on:startup, button:any, set(str:func_name, &quot;button:any, on:a, print(hello); print(world?!)&quot;)'&#10;And then you can call this &quot;function&quot; by doing: call(func_name)&#10;The actions inside the function will literally be parsed as if they are written in place, so the self element is the one that runs call()!&#10;IT EVEN SUPPORTS ARGUMENTS!&#10;You can pass in arguments like this: call(func_name, [arg1, arg2...])&#10;It's parsed like any other field so you can do the same wild math as everywhere else.&#10;In the function, you can use the args by using the 'args' variable, which is just an array, so indexing the args works like: 'args.1' or 'args.9' or 'args.0'. Or even 'args.x' or 'args.r', like the normal parser does.&#10;&#10;[Minor]&#10;Added 'trigger:' filter which defines on which cue the button:&quot;KeyBind or Combo&quot; should run, like, on release of the key or repeat or down or press...&#10;&#10;Fixed parsing of multiple actions after one another, now syntax is proper with either space or semicolon between actions!&#10;&#10;You can now open or close an array of menu names or just one!&#10;I define some menus:&#10;```&#10;global_actions:&#10;     # Menus for each screen&#10;     - button:a, on:startup in:any, set(str:main_menus, [MainMenu]);&#10;     - button:a, on:startup in:any, set(str:settings_menus, [Settings]);&#10;     - button:a, on:startup in:any, set(str:play_menus, [GUI]);&#10;     - button:a, on:startup in:any, set(str:editor_menus, [Editor_Menu, EditorGUI]);&#10;```&#10;And you can just use open_menu(main_menus) to open the main menus&#10;&#10;Fixed the {} substitution not substituting settings-based variables! So using a variable that is a setting wouldn't give you the correct result! Like in here:&#10;- button:&quot;Toggle editor mode&quot; trigger:repeat in:any, toggle(str:editor_mode); if({editor_mode}, call(open_editor_menus));&#10;In here, {editor_mode} would have failed, so it would be false, because editor_mode is a setting.&#10;I applied the same fix to the expression parser so it is consistent everywhere.&#10;&#10;Made add_element() action evaluate menu, layer and id as string_to_value() like it should be, like everywhere.&#10;Same for clone(), clone_layer(), delete_layer() and delete().&#10;&#10;Fixed input, because when I fetch the state of keybind_released, I was mutating it in place and the second time literally gave false everytime even though it was in the same tick, because I mutated it like that!&#10;&#10;added self.offset_order which you can set to an integer value to shift the position of the element in question back and forth compared to other UI elements.&#10;&#10;I am now suppressing the annoying ALSA errors by hijacking the stderr and filtering this garbage out. Audio worked anyway. Only on linux.&#10;&#10;Made the frame count start after frame 0 finished and made game start be frame 0.&#10;&#10;Fixed some UI blending issue with blur, maybe! Always maybe... Not always!&#10;&#10;unactive elements now also get Always events so actions that need on:always or on:a or on:startup work now!&#10;The pressable field now makes elements transparent to touches if false.&#10;&#10;Added 'a' to the component index function so you can now index arrays with 'arr.a', which is 'arr[3]' because rgba.&#10;&#10;You can set the actions of elements with set(str:self.actions, [str]) now, with one action or an array.&#10;I fixed the zoning demand indicator through all these fixes.&#10;&#10;You can now do math between two array in the expression!&#10;For example: - on:drag button:any in:any, set(str:self.center, ({mouse_pos}+{drag_offset}));&#10;Here, each pair of values gets add up and put into a new array, any unpaired values will be passed on.&#10;Same goes for multiply and for subtract, oh by the way, subtract is cleaner in the code.&#10;&#10;Added EditorGUI Menu, beginning to make a GUI for editing, UI is becoming mature.&#10;&#10;Saving a Save with an empty name will now yield a correct error, not attempt to save.&#10;&#10;***&#10;Oh shit I forgot that I already told you about the 'as:' support! Bruh!!! Wait no, I actually did NOT!&#10;&#10;Ok goals for the next version include:&#10;Making scaling based on 1920x1080, prime priority.&#10;That means All coords and sizes will be based on Full HD, rather than 0..1 normalized screen space!&#10;This will ensure that squares will be square and scaling MAKES SENSE!&#10;Right now, the UI scales awkwardly!&#10;&#10;This is a GIGANTIC update, mainly for UI of course! But saving is super important.&#10;I love that I cleaned up bullshit like the ALSA errors!&#10;I won't write a story here, the commit is long enough!&#10;But let me tell you that it is a breeze! This update is so goddamn important and hits so many pain points I had with UI, now I can use it much more easily and correctly!&#10;It is pleasant to code in! Until I hit a weird issue that leads me to a bug hunt... But hey, I solve the bugs!&#10;Idk, I wanna keep talking, but I don't know what to say.&#10;&#10;Signed-off-by: maxwag9 &lt;maximwagner46@gmail.com&gt;" />
    <MESSAGE value="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.8.2a July 15th 22:31&#10;&#10;[Major]&#10;Fixed some of the legacy road crashes from before, a lot still remains.&#10;&#10;Fixed major UI parsing issue, now pingpong and zoning demand indicators work again!&#10;&#10;[Minor]&#10;Fixed some parking things, but the car freezes when in parking mode, so until later!&#10;&#10;Added knockback to the paddles in the Ping Pong menu.&#10;Added ball squish when it touches the paddles in the Ping Pong menu.&#10;&#10;The set zoning type buttons now switch the cursor mode to zoning.&#10;&#10;***&#10;That's kind of it? Bruh." />
    <MESSAGE value="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.8.4a August 2nd 11:34 (now 15:28)&#10;&#10;More UI updates, and trees!&#10;Updated render manager to 30.0.2.&#10;&#10;[Major]&#10;Added natural tree spawning, happens when chunks generate. The trees cluster into forests smoothly!&#10;Improved tree LOD distances and adapted the models to be cheaper, also made tree billboards look better.&#10;&#10;Improved Props rendering (trees are props btw) to not send buffers every frame. I had to update the buffers every frame because I did the WorldPos relative math and the lod distance selection on CPU, which is completely ridiculous.&#10;So I moved the WorldPos to render pos calculation to per vertex in the shader instead!&#10;Problem is that lod selection is now only per chunk, so that I can upload whole chunks instead of per tree, a necessary compromise for now.&#10;I will compute LODs in compute shaders in the future, brace yourself. I want millions of trees.&#10;&#10;Added the slider advanced primitive, which is a slider.&#10;For that, I changed the ap_var of the Advanced element to ap_vars instead, so you can pass multiple ap vars, accessing them using {ap.n}, it is just an array after all.&#10;&#10;I can now use the gizmo from anywhere, because I added a global vector that stores pending gizmo renders that gets drained every frame by the real gizmo.&#10;&#10;Changed the entire UI to be FullHD based, so coords and sizes stored in YAML are as if the screen is 1920x1080 pixels.&#10;This makes it way easier to understand and scale, as well as not morphing with aspect ratio changes, so a square stays square.&#10;&#10;Added COLOR GRADING!You can set the Color grade in the setting, aswell as the tonemapping, so now you have two tonemapping pass settings!&#10;There is a &quot;Mexican&quot; preset, try it out! (Orange breaking bad mexico scene kind of color grading!)&#10;&#10;The ui actions 'call()' action can now call rust functions, using the 'rust:' prefix as in: 'call(rust:str:function_name, [args])'.&#10;This allows me to call rust functions I defined as callable, like in   - on:startup in:any, call(rust:str:get_saves);&#10;Which calls the get_saves() Rust function and puts the result in the variable called 'saves'.&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;[Minor]&#10;You can access Info about all Saves in the saves folder using the 'saves' variable now.&#10;It returns a Vec&lt;Vec&lt;(name, load_result, timestamp_unix, chunk_size)&gt;&gt;&#10;&#10;Migrated some UI menus and APs to fullhd based, but haven't changed them all yet.&#10;&#10;Added 'on:' event filters: on:screen_resize, on:drag_start and on:drag_end&#10;&#10;Now, button:any/button:a is the default if no button: filter was specified, instead of button:left. This will let me stop writing 'button:a' everywhere!&#10;&#10;Turned on UI saving again, idk why I turned it off, fear of breaking UI?&#10;&#10;I am now tracking Settings changes within a frame, like for example changing the MSAA sample count in the settings, because if it does change, I absolutely have to call some functions so that wgpu doesn't crash my game!&#10;&#10;Added MipmapMode to my render manager, hence the update. &#10;This allows me to specify how I want the mipmaps to be generated, be it having None.&#10;Or by Generating all mip maps by generating the procedural texture again for each level, or by downsampling the texture... &#10;And also a KeepAlpha kind of mipmap generation, for foliage. (Trees!)&#10;&#10;Fixed dropdown show interaction call. No shadows enabled there, because they just spawn infinitely just in that case, I must investigate.&#10;Also made the text on the dropdown not touchable, so that you don't accidentally press the text instead of the option, the text must stay information only here!&#10;&#10;Changed Gizmo struct so that I can create an empty one, just to use it in difficult places where I can't have access to the real Gizmo struct mutably.&#10;I can create an empty Gizmo and just use it as if it is the real one, then send the pending renders from the empty gizmo out to the global gizmo pending renders vector.&#10;The real gizmo will pull and render them, completing the process! &#10;&#10;Added settings.print_parse_errors setting, and I am now deduplicating ParseErrors!&#10;&#10;Improved the vignette to look correct on any aspect ratio. Before, it was just a circle.&#10;&#10;Fixed text editing quiting when clicking on the text while editing it.&#10;Made all elements touchable in editor_mode.&#10;&#10;***&#10;Big update? No, just a normal update. It just seems big because for some reason I take longer and longer time to commit. This one took 9 days or 10? Depends on your philosophical view point.&#10;&#10;If your chess grandmaster was Plato, you would say 10 days.&#10;But if your Judo 9th Dan teacher was Aristotelis, you would say 9 days, because all good things are 9. Even little girls. Oh, shit you really said that, didn't you?&#10;But in reality, it was always 9.5 days. No 9 or 10 days.&#10;If your teacher was Aristotelis, I would tell you it took 9.50000000000 days.&#10;If your teacher was Plato, I would tell you it took 9.49999999999 days.&#10;Why? Because fuck you!&#10;Just like Mary Klein said in the Backrooms movie!&#10;And that's why Clark survived (He didn't)." />
    <MESSAGE value="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.8.5a August 13th 22:13&#10;&#10;Added 6 goddamn crates: sysinfo, gfxinfo, glyphon, wow_colors, unicode_segmentation, fontdb&#10;&#10;[Major]&#10;Completely switched the UI text renderer from wgpu_text to glyphon. But the 3D text of the Gizmo stays wgpu_text. &#10;That's why I removed that crate and then added it again because I realized Gizmo uses it too!&#10;Now all text has a 1 pixel large black border whether you want it or not.&#10;This is because I have been trying out how to make borders work, because glyphon ALSO doesn't support it!&#10;So, behind the scenes, I forked glyphon and wll probably fork cosmic-text too, so that I can add text border capability. &#10;I already started, but I don't have the time because I am going to Croatia for 2 weeks tomorrow.&#10;So it is not in the game, I use Vanilla Glyphon right now,a nd the border is being done by rendering the same text in black 8 more times in every cardinal direction. Temporary crap that works.&#10;It looks awesome btw, I want it in my game. Ok enough of this.&#10;&#10;Made all UI elements write and use the UI depth buffer so that order matters. So that text can be behind a rectangle and be obscured, and not on top of everything!&#10;While I added this feature, it is disabled by making the CompareFunction to ::Always so it doesn't compare, because it is very buggy at the moment.&#10;I need to sort some stuff out, mainly layer order collisions, for which I want to find an ergonomic and simple solution.&#10;&#10;Added FullscreenMode! You can switch between Fullscreen, Borderless and Windowed in the settings menu! (BTW! In wayland, Fullscreen doesn't exist!! It just doesn't! And that's good!)&#10;&#10;I made ALL expressions in the actions arguments EXPLICIT, using 'expr:1+1' for anything that wants to go through the expensive Tokenizer/AST/Evaluator Parser!!&#10;Restructured from_str() to remove the expression at the end and move it to the explicit path, so now, from_str() will make String the fallback.&#10;Made certain explicit types like 'bool:' accept more options than the non-explicit path.&#10;&#10;COMPLETELY changed the entire *fucking* parser from a stupid little prick (tokenizer, then evaluator) to a PROPER behemoth (only slightly bigger, tokenizer, then AST, then evaluator).&#10;The error messages in the parser are 400% better and even builtin functions have error messages now!&#10;The parser syntax has been completely changed to be much more explicit.&#10;It now disallows random stray shit, it will just error if you do, sometimes, it depends, idk.&#10;If you want to get a variable or setting, you must wrap the name in curly braces: '{msaa_samples}' in the parser.&#10;and tons of other changes that are super important.&#10;&#10;I am now printing super usefull condensed, dense lines of System Information, basically anything you want to know about your system is there.&#10;And it prints some funny stuff about your RAM amount!&#10;&#10;[Minor]&#10;Added the Pause Menu! It pops up when you are inside a Save and press escape, so you get into the pause menu instead of the Main menu!&#10;I still have to change the settings back to the main menu buttons and of other menus like pingpong...&#10;&#10;Added a simple &quot;button&quot; Advanced Primitive (widget basically but not really yk).&#10;It serves to make all buttons across the game UI more unified in look and behaviour and makes it easier for myself to add buttons.&#10;&#10;Fixed slider AP fully, it now fully works and behaves like I want it to. Explicit options, Aliases for these options, the options are optional, the slider can be exponential or linear And more.&#10;&#10;Added SavesScreen.&#10;The saves screen is very much in shambles at the moment, as it waits for the pending major changes (depth and text borders).&#10;The saves screen shows the saves with their info and how long ago it was saved and has a reload button and play save button and more non functioning buttons. &#10;&#10;Made changes in parsing of inner content of actions (arguments, mainly to prevent action-looking-thingies inside the arguments of actions being misread as actions.)&#10;Also now not parsing filters when inside command/string.&#10;&#10;Fixed shadows and other things inside show_interaction().&#10;&#10;Made it possible to set the text or template of a text element. (setting the text is useles... The template is converted and text overwritten.)&#10;Also exposed the text and template as variables. (self.text/self.template/as.template)&#10;&#10;Changed the keybinds to be explicit by default, which means only exactly the key combo &quot;Shift+KeyA&quot; works. You can make it independent of any extra modifiers pressed by adding an exclammation mark: &quot;Shift+KeyA!&quot;.&#10;Then you can hold CTRL+Shift+KeyA and it will fire, but without '!' it won't!&#10;&#10;Heavily modified car parking, but some big issues remain, doesn't park yet, maybe. Mostly. 99.69% Mostly doesn't park.&#10;I am rendering whatever the car is thinking when parking (It's not that deep bruh)&#10;&#10;Made all instances of SAFE road node/lane/segment fetching from the road storage instead use the unwrap() version so that it panics when some bullshit with the ids happened.&#10;Fixed nearly all the legacy road id problems. Some crashes still remain but idk, haven't noticed more yet, because A CERTAIN SUBSYSTEM *cough* UI PARSING *cough* TOOK UP MY WHOLE TIME!!&#10;&#10;I am now registering the archetypes of the forest trees when they appear, so they now appear in game. Prior to this, you had to place your own tree for the archetype to be registered so you could even see the forest.&#10;&#10;Made the debug menu not touchable.&#10;Made the leave game and exit to main menu/pause menu keybinds also accept MouseBack as the key to fire.&#10;&#10;Changed lots of menus and aps to the new Fullhd scale coordinate system. The editor menu remains.&#10;&#10;Made Save names safe&#10;I am now MAYBE measuring CPU time correctly, instead of including the wait of getting the gpu frame.&#10;&#10;The present mode selection fallbacks are now better.&#10;&#10;Fixed suboptimal surface frame from wgpu crashing (because I configured the surface, even though wgpu literally told me not to!!)&#10;&#10;Made ap_vars vars go through a pass of from_str() before substituting all placeholders.&#10;&#10;Now UI elements store cache, not layers. And I exposed the text width and height of the entire text as 'self.size'.&#10;&#10;***&#10;I just finished writing the commit, it is 23:29, I have work tomorrow at 6:25.&#10;Fuck, no sleep.&#10;&#10;Anyway, here is a useless but cool story:&#10;One day, Gizmo was walking around in a park all by himself, being benign and happy and living in the moment.&#10;Then suddenly, maxwag9 came and took away its wgpu_text.&#10;Gizmo was absolutely furious and turned into Goku.&#10;Then maxwag9 just flew away to Japan and ripped out wgpu_text, ripped out of the UI text pipeline. And then threw it in the fire.&#10;And then boiled it and then crushed it beneath a concrete wall (wtf?).&#10;Maxwag9 then said: &quot;All done!&quot;. He went back to program and stole a Glyphon from the store nearby and implemented it into his (MINE!! MY PRECIOUS!) game.&#10;&#10;BUT THEN!&#10;Out of NOWHERE, Gizmo gives him an upper cut and leaves him on the floor.&#10;Then maxwag9 (The real one) descends from heaven and places his ass gently on the computer chair and adds wgpu_text back to cargo.toml, making Gizmo happy.&#10;The rust compiler also became happy, kinda.&#10;The fake maxwag9 then got dragged into heaven against his will and got recycled there, idk what that means.&#10;But at least no Amongus appeared in this story!&#10;The end." />
    <MESSAGE value="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.8.6a August 31st 21:04 now 22:24&#10;&#10;[Major]&#10;NUMBER ONE FIX: Fixed glyphon UI text being garbage after resizing! The positions were shifting super weirdly and the resolution of the text was lacking!&#10;Guess what the cause was?&#10;When I updated the glyphon viewport to the new resolution, I accidentally, for some FUCKING REASON, used the 'self.old_window_size' instead of the 'new_size'! WTF?? How the fuck could I have missed this?&#10; Was I asleep? WHAT THE FUCK? &#10; I was so shocked when I saw this, because I looked at the resizing function like 8 times and missed this shit, until I pasted half my game to CLAUDE of all AIs and he/she/it pointed 11 fingers at this cause!&#10;Anyway.&#10;Made player-to-district distance calculation be accurate, instead of making the distance using the district center, I test against all the district segments of its bounds.&#10;This makes it more obvious in which district you currently are!&#10;And to make it even more obvious (actually obvious visually rather than by feeling), I am drawing a red border around the current district!&#10;&#10;Changed the UI actions execution order.&#10;It was executing all actions per event, but now it is executing all actions and testing events!&#10;This means that when you write a list of actions in an element, and you expect it to execute from top to bottom, you can now be sure it does.&#10;I also split Element Events and Global events properly, but of course they must still intersect.&#10;&#10;Added CreateSave.yaml, in which you can select the difficulty and type in a world name and create a new Save!&#10;&#10;Now properly tracking cpu time and providing more detailed variables for where the cpu frametime is going (UI needs 8ms alone for rendering and logic and parsing and whatever, which is horrible!!)&#10;&#10;Fixed text editing for any text edit! Now editing text works exactly as I imagined.&#10;And also made input boxes work now, after over half a year of being a dead feature in the text!&#10;Of course the world name is an input box.&#10;&#10;[Minor]&#10;Added controls: saturation, brightness, contrast, exposure, vignette_strength, vignette_radius and vignette_softness!&#10;These controls are interesting.&#10;&#10;Added F11 fullscreen key support!&#10;Made the &quot;Fullscreen&quot; option loop back to &quot;Borderless&quot; on Wayland, because Wayland doesn't have an exclusive Fullscreen mode. &#10;And that's for the better. (*Injecting random highly controversial opinions to subconsciously influence reader*) But it isn't controversial.&#10;Made Toggle work for Enums in settings. So the toggle() action can cycle the enums.&#10;toggle() is now much more resilient to existing variables that aren't bool.&#10;&#10;One can now edit border sizes of elements.&#10;Changed border thickness from percentage based to 1080p pixel based.&#10;Changed the checkbox completely, gave it a whole new style.&#10;&#10;Moved total_game_time into saves, because OF COURSE every world needs its own time ofc!&#10;Added difficulty into saves.&#10;Showing Game Version in the top left of the debug menu, just like in minecraft!&#10;Fixed dropdown and slider.&#10;Fixed the pause circle button and made the GUI background become RED to visualize that the game is paused!&#10;Fixed money text and all the texts in the GUI.&#10;Fixed input &quot;just_pressed&quot; not being cleared until it's being read, possibly seconds later.&#10;Added support for precision in from_str(), so to prevent constant usage of 'expr:', improving performance with dozens of texts like in the debug menu.&#10;Removed input snapshots from UI, using Input directly instead.&#10;&#10;Made MiscButtonSettingsYaml and its fields serialize away more.&#10;Made zoning_demand_indicator simpler internally and rounder externally!&#10;&#10;***&#10;I came from my two-week vacation in croatia in Ŝilo, Krk. It was awesome as always, I and my family are there quite frequently, like every couple of years...&#10;And always the same house. The house is pretty old and has kinda run down apartments that we had to clean, but two weeks cost 1200€ in this very expensive area, so not complaining.&#10;My mom found a hut in Ŝilo that is 3000€... Just a hut! But it would have been a good hut so whatever.&#10;I programmed just a small bit over there. The transfer commit knows.&#10;&#10;A small story at the end:&#10;Every time you look at your keyboard, you might see a key called &quot;Alt Gr&quot;. If you don't, you belong to the very common group.&#10;But if you do see that key, then you belong to the 0.0000239% of people in the world, you are a chosen one.&#10;Not the chosen one, just a.&#10;This is because with the power of Alt Gr, you can do wonderful things that the common plebians can't do.&#10;For instance, you can type &quot;@&quot; and &quot;€&quot; very simply, while the plebians must consult the holy www!&#10;Another perk is that it is Alt+Ctrl, so now you have a shortcut for when you only have two fingers after some War.&#10;If you belong to this epic minority, contact me on discord. (Germans included)" />
    <MESSAGE value="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.8.7a September 9th 20:22&#10;&#10;[Major]&#10;HUGE UI ACTIONS PERFORMANCE UPDATE&#10;I am now COMPILING UI Actions, which just means that when I load actions from elements when elements get loaded, I &quot;compile&quot; them.&#10;That just means that the work I did before is now cached and reused, as it should be.&#10;The work from before: &#10;1. Take all actions I need for this frame and clone them.&#10;2. Split off and parse the filters&#10;3. Parse the rest, so split the individual ui actions and parse them each. The values are not parsed ofc.&#10;4. Next frame, repeat this for every element and action.&#10;&#10;Now though:&#10;1. Take all the elements that can have actions running right now.&#10;2. Use the compiled actions&#10;3. Profit multiple ms of CPU time PER FRAME&#10;&#10;Inactive elements now don't run actions, wait no, they do, but whatever.&#10;&#10;Added 'scope:' filter, which controls whether the action can be run always, or only on active elements. I think. Most likely, I forgot. Already obscure.&#10;Added 'asdyn:' as an analogue to 'as:'. The difference is that asdyn is like before, but just 'as' is now STATIC, so it can't do expressions or variables or settings.&#10;This was required so that I can compile 'as:' aswell.&#10;&#10;Another HUGE performance improvement, maybe even larger than the compilation:&#10;I changed element property lookup to on-demand.&#10;Before:&#10;1. Send ALL element properties of self and as to VARIABLES.&#10;2. Read them from variables.&#10;NOW:&#10;1. Read variables&#10;2. STOP!! Before I let you fetch this &quot;variable&quot;, as you like to call it, from the variables, let me interest you in some element properties! I've got only the finest ones! Come on in!&#10;3. If it is a name that wants something from an element, then get that specific value, else, get the variable.&#10;&#10;This saves like 3000 Hashmap WRITES per frame.&#10;Idk how many it really is, because it depends on how many actions the entire UI has and how many times from_str() is called on them.&#10;The compiled UI action is &quot;run&quot; which means matching the UICommand and converting all the String to Value using from_str(), so yes, the arguments of UI actions are NOT compiled!&#10;So let's say we have 300 from_str calls that ACTUALLY get somewhere where they need to get a variable.&#10;&#10;Oh holy shit, wait. &#10;I just looked up and the send_element_properties_to_variables() function is called on EVERY string_to_value that the UICommand does!&#10;I don't think it affects expression parsing though, it fetched differently before.&#10;&#10;Ok so 300 string_to_value() this frame, and like 23 to 29 Hashmap writes per string_to_value(), so 6900 to 8700 HASHMAP *WRITES* per frame.&#10;At 60 FPS: 414000 to 522000 Hashmap writes.&#10;The CPU hates this shit, because RAM IS SLOW!!!&#10;Now all of that is gone.&#10;&#10;Added ploppable buildings, so you can add a new Building with a YAML file and place it in-game.&#10;Right now, there is literally 0 ergonomics and 0 UI that controls this, you just press 'F' and the one building I let ChatGPT create, the &quot;Aurora Spire&quot;, gets built.&#10;No previews or whatever!! All in the next update.&#10;&#10;Added SFX!! You can define a sound effect using, again, YAML! As always... I love it?&#10;The SFX has a name and ADSR and gain, pan, glide curve, duration, including deduplication time.&#10;And the most important part is 'layers', which have a certain Waveform and the start/end frequency and frequency modulation ratio and amount. Each layer has its own gain too.&#10;This is enough for some good sound effects. You can add a sound effect conditionally in the elements' actions, using call(RUST:play_sound, str:ButtonHover)&#10;Then you have a file that defines the sound effect 'ButtonHover'.&#10;&#10;I already added some sounds, like ButtonHover, Backspace, DragRoad, PlaceRoad, ButtonPress, Write...&#10;The DragRoad sound effect is just like in Cities Skylines. You place a road point, then drag it out, and if the length of the road changed by 2m or more since the last time the sound was played, then it plays the sound. Tick tick tick tick tic-...&#10;&#10;Added resize behaviour to UI elements.&#10;    resize_behaviour:&#10;      width: X/Y/Uniform/None&#10;      height: X/Y/Uniform/None&#10;This makes it actually possible to control how each element resizes!&#10;I already fixed The settings, main and GUI menus to be perfectly resizable! (With edge cases, ofc...)&#10;Yes this is &quot;Major&quot;, suck the major if you didn't expect it (What I mean by that is going to a casino and wherever you see the word &quot;MAJOR&quot;, suckle that spot. I am not liable for any diabetes transmitted by this act)&#10;&#10;Forked sluggrs, an experimental text renderer without atlas textures and better performance, and added Text border support to it.&#10;Then refactored my game slightly to use sluggrs, or rather, my fork, sluggrs_skylines. Who would have thought.&#10;So now I ahve text border support in my game! Teh borders are very clean, with a tiny amount of edge cases, mainly in large borders.&#10;You can, of course, choose any color you want.&#10;&#10;This is a big positive change, because I was just about ready to fork glyphon and dissect it and add sdf atlas textures and add border support like that. Thank god this didn't happen.&#10;I can also add text background very easily. If you want it! (Not done yet, I am still waiting for your response, do you want it or not?)&#10;&#10;[Minor]&#10;Added a custom mouse cursor for absolutely no reason.&#10;&#10;Made naming of CPU frametimes better, and they are now averaged over half a second and displayed each half second.&#10;Updated winit from 0.31.0-beta.2 to 0.31.0-beta.3, legendary drop.&#10;Got rid of the ShowInteraction UI Action, instead, it is now done through a UI-native solution, using call().&#10;Added difficulty to save headers.&#10;&#10;Upgraded the Road building previews a tiny bit, fixed road crashes, caused by delete_lane() and wrong ordering of impact_of_deleting_x.&#10;Made lots of code in the road editor much clearer and cleaner. Tuples into structs.&#10;Lots of fixes for the neglected curved roads, especially the closest_point_to() calculations that snapping relied on.&#10;Added button to build Curved roads or Straight roads in the middle of the screen. Yes, I could change it right now, but I would like you to see it.&#10;So now you can build curved roads.&#10;&#10;Added a large, simple &quot;RUSTY SKYLINES&quot; splash screen. Nothing special, not a logo, just crappy text. But, the large text consumed NO ATLAS SPACE NOW, because there is no atlas texture now!!!!!!&#10;Added saturate() expression function.&#10;Added support for null coalescence with value substitution in the expression parser. You can use expr: {age??18} to get the age, or just use 18 if the age doesn't exist. That's how Pxxxxhiles work.&#10;&#10;Added &quot;Exit World and Save&quot; button to Pause menu.&#10;Fixed any atlas texture issues with UI text by using .trim()&#10;&#10;***&#10;Me: Plebians. A reddit mods' favorite word. &#10;Reddit mod: Uhm actually, it is 'Plebeians' you ignorant fuck!! Or dare I say, &quot;you Plebeian&quot;, heh heh *Tips fedora* *Uses Belle Delphine Linux though, not fedora*&#10;&#10;RSUIDSL, guess what that means. Rusty Skylines User Interface Domain-Specific Language&#10;&#10;E pluribus unum&#10;Unum e pluribus. Walker ah no, ranger ah no, reacher!&#10;&#10;Weird aldecaldos-style NPC beach music playing (Jealous by Faydee) Fuck, no, it is not aldecaldos, it is Valentinos! Or just spanish-style despacito beat.&#10;No coding Scheme today. Only pyramids. Like Mr hands. Wtf am I talking bout'" />
    <MESSAGE value="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.8.8a September 15th 15:42&#10;&#10;[Major]&#10;Made the ploppable buildings properly ploppable! Now, when you click the Buildings button, the preview is started and follows your mouse, you can rotate it using the right mouse button held or the forward/backward mouse buttons.&#10;Then you can place it down with the left mouse button, and it becomes a building just like any other, but of course with some specialties later.&#10;The building can snap to the roads and fill in spaces between other lots.&#10;You can cancel building the building with ESC.&#10;And if I remember correctly, in the last version, the building didn't draw at all. Yes it didn't there was no preview. Win!&#10;&#10;Big update to the lot fitting!&#10;Now when you drag to zone lots, they automatically vary in size and fill in gaps between lots so every m² gets used.&#10;The lots hug the roads and curved roads and curve with the roads and can also be non-rectangular.&#10;Much better than just one rectangle size for all lots with gaps and everything!&#10;&#10;Improved the SFX immensely, not the sound effects themselves kinda, but the actual system.&#10;I moved the ADSR and panning and other settings into each SFXLayer and added some good global settings.&#10;I also added low pass and high pass filtering per layer and delay for each layer, so you can actually change when a layer plays.&#10;I also added a new waveform: 'Pulse' and the pulse_width.&#10;&#10;Completely refactored the Building Mesher so that it is much more modular and less repetitive in code.&#10;All UVs were fixed too so that they aren't stretched!!&#10;And the mesh has WAY FEWER vertices now, because I am actually greedy meshing it instead of having a quad per tile or a quad per vertical run!&#10;But buildings still look roughly the same.&#10;&#10;Made the LotLayout also much more modular and less duplicated code and such.&#10;&#10;Added First person mode to the camera, you can switch between Orbit and FPV modes using 'F4'!&#10;It isn't a mode where oyu can run around yet, you still fly just like in Orbit, but you just orbit at like 0 distance basically.&#10;There is a bug with the 3D Gizmo Text in FPV mode, because the text size changes based on your orbit.&#10;&#10;Added texture support to UI Rects!&#10;You can do: &#10;texture: &quot;shader:shaders/fun!/test.wgsl&quot;&#10;or&#10;texture: &quot;texture:textures/pointer.png&quot;&#10;And it will show the texture on the whole rect (With the border/fill and everything drawn on top)&#10;Or use the shader to draw using the shader, duh.&#10;I have made 4 test shaders in &quot;rustycity/data/shaders/fun!/&quot; with ChatGPT.&#10;I support exclamation marks in Paths.&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;[Minor]&#10;Fixed Editor mode not toggling.&#10;&#10;Heavily (maybe) improved simulation performance by caching the floor area of each lot instead of calculating it every time I need it (Which would read one whole Hashmap of LotTiles to get the area).&#10;&#10;Completely removed the useless ChunkId: u64 from my project.&#10;&#10;Added PlaceBuilding SFX and improved several others.&#10;&#10;Fixed multiple bug inside the Props system related to some Sync issues between the PropInstance position and the PropChunk it is in.&#10;&#10;Added &quot;Audio Jungle&quot; button to the MainMenu so I can quickly test sounds.&#10;&#10;Fixed the Gizmo Arrow start-stopper and head being out of proportion compared to the arrow line.&#10;&#10;***&#10;Added amogus to cargo.toml: &quot;#glyphon = &quot;0.12.0&quot; ඞ&quot; glyphon is commented out. -i don't# u se it aymore&#10;&#10;Time for another story.&#10;One day, amogus was walking blissfully in space, then he fucking died from hypothermia or asphyxiation.&#10;The end.&#10;Next day, 3 Imposters and 8944 crewmates boarded USS Titanic (United States Spaceship 'Titanic')&#10;They flew quite quickly and reached pluto in just a few years.&#10;Then the imposters have already killed 5666 crewmates without anyone noticing, because they made all deaths look natural.&#10;One evening (Whatever that means), 3 Amogi flew by and all the crewmates looked out of the 5666 windows (how convenient) to watch them fly by.&#10;Then they looked back and saw that the three imposters did not look out of the window and were just standing there like nothing happened.&#10;The Captain FUCKING SNAPPED and used his dirty Sailor mouth to speak of such atrocities at the three imposters...&#10;BTW, the crewmates didn't know for sure that they were imposters. But now they can't deny that it is SUS!!!&#10;So they threw the three out and watched them fly by through the windows.&#10;Then, by some cosmic miracle, the 1 Amogus who died in Space happens to collide with the 3 Imposters (The three imposters were bundled tightly together).&#10;Then the crewmates finally settled on pluto and lived happily ever after... Until the 3 imposters came back...&#10;You see, the one amogus had a way higher speed than the three imposters, and when they collided, they got flung right into the direction of pluton, perfectly on course to land on pluto after a few months.&#10;Imposters handle space isolation way better than normal Amogi.&#10;Amogi can only survive for a few days at best, but imposters can do months.&#10;So when they landed... Mayhem.&#10;The end. For real." />
    <MESSAGE value="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.9.0a September 27th 21:07&#10;&#10;Formerly Alpha v1.8.9&#10;&#10;[Major]&#10;Added modding support!&#10;I am calling this &quot;Soft Mod&quot; support, because these mods are just YAML files!&#10;It is stronger than Minecraft resource packs, but weaker than Minecraft Datapacks!&#10;It works like this:&#10;1. You make a new folder and put it in the Rusty Skylines folder in '/Documents/Rusty Skylines/', or wherever my game decided to put that folder (COULD BE beside the .minecraft folder in Appdata/Roaming!)&#10;2. Look at my Base mod in the Game files, under the data directory. It is the exact same as any mod, just made by me and sits in the game files, its structure is how you can make your mod, and also look inside the files to get the syntax.&#10;3. Make directories and files of whatever you want, stuff gets replaced when loading the game.&#10;4. Profit&#10;&#10;For now, in this update, you can't yet control the ordering of soft mods and enabled/disable them...&#10;&#10;Added utilities!&#10;So now you can define any utilities you like in your mod!&#10;I added Electricity.yaml and Clean Water.yaml already!&#10;I didn't really test the utilities yet, I programmed them though... &#10;There should be bottleneck detection, automatic utilities network pathfinding on topology change and the consumers/producers which for now are just the buildings.&#10;Each lane of a road has n amount of 'Rails', where 'n' is the total number of utilities. So every road, no matter how small, can definitely transfer all utilities.&#10;A utility like Electricity can use multiple rails to meet demand, to transfer the electricity to the consumers from the producers.&#10;In the future, there will be secondary unit support, which will allow concepts like Voltage in Electricity to require you to build actual transformers, electrical infrastructure.&#10;&#10;Made SFX support WAY stronger, you can define notes in multiple layers and have actual controls over bpm and bars and such!&#10;There are like 2 songs I let AI make because I really don't care about music that much and don't even know how the notes system works exactly, because I let ChatGPT vibe code it.&#10;Also fixed the timing between the layers.&#10;&#10;Gizmo text has been turned 2D.&#10;I migrated it to sluggrs_skylines, just like my UI uses, so that it is consistent and I have less packages in my cargo.toml.&#10;In the last version, Gizmo text used wgpu_text and a custom 3D shader to position it.&#10;With sluggrs, it has exactly the same capabilities as UI text.&#10;&#10;[Minor]&#10;Updated sluggrs_skylines to reflect the new version of sluggrs.&#10;This means that every text in the game, including Gizmo text now, has decorations: [TextDecoration] ability!&#10;This means shadows in any direction and color, outlines of any size and color and rings of any size and color!&#10;The performance cost seems negligible!&#10;You can stack lots of decoration onto each other!&#10;This version is limited edition, because it includes like 8 text decorations stacked onto each other for the text of the 'button.yaml' Advance Primitive!&#10;That makes every button text look *colorful*!! OOH wooh WOOH&#10;&#10;Made Road Regions work now! &#10;Previously, the Road regions would get out of sync immediately, of course, because there was no pathfinding that updated when topology changed! &#10;The road regions were tracked purely additively, but splitting was impossible!&#10;Now the UtilityNetwork pathfinds the road network to find out where utilities are present and while doing that, runs bottle neck checks and of course just writes the result to the Road Regions, because it's literally the same thing.&#10;&#10;Fixed add_raw() in the RoadStorage.&#10;Improved car model, but buggy.&#10;Added &quot;stop_sounds&quot; rust command for UI call action. Stops all sounds.&#10;Added MiniGames.yaml menu, containing a short description and different rect shader from THE FUN! FOLDER! It contains PingPong! Cool.&#10;&#10;That's kind of it...&#10;&#10;***&#10;I have 'Hard Mods' planned soon!&#10;I am very envious of Minecraft's modding ecosystem, so much power with their mixins and whatever!!&#10;So I thought a bit...&#10;My game is written in rust, which is compiled, so people can't really edit the binary source code, that would be completely bonkers and inefficient and literally game-breaking and segfault-inducing!&#10;Java, which I recently started liking instead of hating, is not really compiled, I mean, it is kinda, but like, mods can inject their material in any class!&#10;That allows modders to replace basically any part of Minecraft completely, or just add to it in certain spots! I think it's like that kinda.&#10;Now I could just provide a very strong API for my soft mods or wasm/lua scripting, but that would be much weaker anyway...&#10;SO MY GENIUS IDEA:&#10;Just fucking compile the game when you change hard mods!&#10;Hard mods will inject RUST code wherever they want and replace any source files they want!&#10;Rusty Skylines will start in a launcher/wrapper that is just some simple egui interface, where you can turn mods on and off and recompile the whole game with mods!&#10;It's like Github with pull requests, but automatic and togglable!&#10;I haven't figured out the code merging yet though... Maybe it will be some kind of Git-style thing and mods just define where to change something...&#10;When the game hits a compile error, the wrapper could show solutions and the player could select some I guess!&#10;The biggest issue though, might be the SECURITY!&#10;Minecraft has its own code merging problems with the mixins, so it's nothing new.&#10;But Minecraft is effectively sandboxed in java!&#10;But RUST is literally just machine code!&#10;A mod is like running a random .exe file you found on the street, so it can do anything that the game has privileges to do.&#10;And without sandboxing, assholes can make mods that steal discord, browser tokens and cookies and more...&#10;So this is the prime focus!&#10;1. I will sandbox the game to the most essential folders only (Rusty Skylines Documents folder and game folder and some drivers I guess)&#10;Sandboxing on linux is baby-easy, but on Windows, it is quite a challenge, and on macOS... Fuck Apple. &#10;macOS will just get a big fat warning label, 'You are completely on your own, apple's fault!'&#10;2. Trusted mods, I will award some mods authenticity if they are legit.&#10;3. You can still load any hard mod you want, like, any! I won't prohibit you, I will jsut make it very obvious that you are entering dangerous territory. BUT ultra powerful territory, probably more than minecraft.&#10;My source code is open-source.&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;BY the way, before I go:&#10;id: Rusty Skylines Mod&#10;name: Rusty Skylines Mod&#10;description: &quot;This is the Base Mod. This is an internal mod, located in the data folder in the game files, which I made. &#10;              This contains basically everything in the game. All UI Menus, shaders, buildings, sfx, utilities, textures and more. &#10;              You can edit it in the data folder like any other mod, because it is 'just another mod'™.&quot;&#10;version: Doesn't matter, idk. 1?&#10;author: maxwag9, the creator of Rusty Skylines" />
    <option name="LAST_COMMIT_MESSAGE" value="Rusty Skylines Alpha v1.9.0a September 27th 21:07&#10;&#10;Formerly Alpha v1.8.9&#10;&#10;[Major]&#10;Added modding support!&#10;I am calling this &quot;Soft Mod&quot; support, because these mods are just YAML files!&#10;It is stronger than Minecraft resource packs, but weaker than Minecraft Datapacks!&#10;It works like this:&#10;1. You make a new folder and put it in the Rusty Skylines folder in '/Documents/Rusty Skylines/', or wherever my game decided to put that folder (COULD BE beside the .minecraft folder in Appdata/Roaming!)&#10;2. Look at my Base mod in the Game files, under the data directory. It is the exact same as any mod, just made by me and sits in the game files, its structure is how you can make your mod, and also look inside the files to get the syntax.&#10;3. Make directories and files of whatever you want, stuff gets replaced when loading the game.&#10;4. Profit&#10;&#10;For now, in this update, you can't yet control the ordering of soft mods and enabled/disable them...&#10;&#10;Added utilities!&#10;So now you can define any utilities you like in your mod!&#10;I added Electricity.yaml and Clean Water.yaml already!&#10;I didn't really test the utilities yet, I programmed them though... &#10;There should be bottleneck detection, automatic utilities network pathfinding on topology change and the consumers/producers which for now are just the buildings.&#10;Each lane of a road has n amount of 'Rails', where 'n' is the total number of utilities. So every road, no matter how small, can definitely transfer all utilities.&#10;A utility like Electricity can use multiple rails to meet demand, to transfer the electricity to the consumers from the producers.&#10;In the future, there will be secondary unit support, which will allow concepts like Voltage in Electricity to require you to build actual transformers, electrical infrastructure.&#10;&#10;Made SFX support WAY stronger, you can define notes in multiple layers and have actual controls over bpm and bars and such!&#10;There are like 2 songs I let AI make because I really don't care about music that much and don't even know how the notes system works exactly, because I let ChatGPT vibe code it.&#10;Also fixed the timing between the layers.&#10;&#10;Gizmo text has been turned 2D.&#10;I migrated it to sluggrs_skylines, just like my UI uses, so that it is consistent and I have less packages in my cargo.toml.&#10;In the last version, Gizmo text used wgpu_text and a custom 3D shader to position it.&#10;With sluggrs, it has exactly the same capabilities as UI text.&#10;&#10;[Minor]&#10;Updated sluggrs_skylines to reflect the new version of sluggrs.&#10;This means that every text in the game, including Gizmo text now, has decorations: [TextDecoration] ability!&#10;This means shadows in any direction and color, outlines of any size and color and rings of any size and color!&#10;The performance cost seems negligible!&#10;You can stack lots of decoration onto each other!&#10;This version is limited edition, because it includes like 8 text decorations stacked onto each other for the text of the 'button.yaml' Advance Primitive!&#10;That makes every button text look *colorful*!! OOH wooh WOOH&#10;&#10;Made Road Regions work now! &#10;Previously, the Road regions would get out of sync immediately, of course, because there was no pathfinding that updated when topology changed! &#10;The road regions were tracked purely additively, but splitting was impossible!&#10;Now the UtilityNetwork pathfinds the road network to find out where utilities are present and while doing that, runs bottle neck checks and of course just writes the result to the Road Regions, because it's literally the same thing.&#10;&#10;Fixed add_raw() in the RoadStorage.&#10;Improved car model, but buggy.&#10;Added &quot;stop_sounds&quot; rust command for UI call action. Stops all sounds.&#10;Added MiniGames.yaml menu, containing a short description and different rect shader from THE FUN! FOLDER! It contains PingPong! Cool.&#10;&#10;That's kind of it...&#10;&#10;***&#10;I have 'Hard Mods' planned soon!&#10;I am very envious of Minecraft's modding ecosystem, so much power with their mixins and whatever!!&#10;So I thought a bit...&#10;My game is written in rust, which is compiled, so people can't really edit the binary source code, that would be completely bonkers and inefficient and literally game-breaking and segfault-inducing!&#10;Java, which I recently started liking instead of hating, is not really compiled, I mean, it is kinda, but like, mods can inject their material in any class!&#10;That allows modders to replace basically any part of Minecraft completely, or just add to it in certain spots! I think it's like that kinda.&#10;Now I could just provide a very strong API for my soft mods or wasm/lua scripting, but that would be much weaker anyway...&#10;SO MY GENIUS IDEA:&#10;Just fucking compile the game when you change hard mods!&#10;Hard mods will inject RUST code wherever they want and replace any source files they want!&#10;Rusty Skylines will start in a launcher/wrapper that is just some simple egui interface, where you can turn mods on and off and recompile the whole game with mods!&#10;It's like Github with pull requests, but automatic and togglable!&#10;I haven't figured out the code merging yet though... Maybe it will be some kind of Git-style thing and mods just define where to change something...&#10;When the game hits a compile error, the wrapper could show solutions and the player could select some I guess!&#10;The biggest issue though, might be the SECURITY!&#10;Minecraft has its own code merging problems with the mixins, so it's nothing new.&#10;But Minecraft is effectively sandboxed in java!&#10;But RUST is literally just machine code!&#10;A mod is like running a random .exe file you found on the street, so it can do anything that the game has privileges to do.&#10;And without sandboxing, assholes can make mods that steal discord, browser tokens and cookies and more...&#10;So this is the prime focus!&#10;1. I will sandbox the game to the most essential folders only (Rusty Skylines Documents folder and game folder and some drivers I guess)&#10;Sandboxing on linux is baby-easy, but on Windows, it is quite a challenge, and on macOS... Fuck Apple. &#10;macOS will just get a big fat warning label, 'You are completely on your own, apple's fault!'&#10;2. Trusted mods, I will award some mods authenticity if they are legit.&#10;3. You can still load any hard mod you want, like, any! I won't prohibit you, I will jsut make it very obvious that you are entering dangerous territory. BUT ultra powerful territory, probably more than minecraft.&#10;My source code is open-source.&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;BY the way, before I go:&#10;id: Rusty Skylines Mod&#10;name: Rusty Skylines Mod&#10;description: &quot;This is the Base Mod. This is an internal mod, located in the data folder in the game files, which I made. &#10;              This contains basically everything in the game. All UI Menus, shaders, buildings, sfx, utilities, textures and more. &#10;              You can edit it in the data folder like any other mod, because it is 'just another mod'™.&quot;&#10;version: Doesn't matter, idk. 1?&#10;author: maxwag9, the creator of Rusty Skylines" />
    <option name="OPTIMIZE_IMPORTS_BEFORE_PROJECT_COMMIT" value="true" />
    <option name="REFORMAT_BEFORE_PROJECT_COMMIT" value="true" />
    <option name="REARRANGE_BEFORE_PROJECT_COMMIT" value="true" />
  </component>
